window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b027-e5e8dd813afa513b.json"]={sha256:"e5e8dd813afa513be76458e95a82698dc8e3a3ebd06a836012461d9bd504a928",value:{"id":"b027","title":"樂天世界塔","titleEn":"Lotte World Tower","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"樂天世界塔高 554.5 m、地上 123 層，以鋼筋混凝土核心筒與八根巨柱承擔重力與側力，兩道外伸臂與多道帶狀桁架把巨柱與核心筒綁在一起，並把頂部斜交網格燈籠與飯店柱轉換到巨柱上。基礎是 6.5 m 厚的筏基，斷層帶以不與筏基相連的補強樁改良地盤。本課沿著重力分擔、外伸臂、巨柱細長效應、帶狀桁架延遲鎖定、筏基一次澆置、預拱、監測與長期潛變，拆解這座韓國最高建築的工程邏輯。","summaryEn":"Lotte World Tower is 554.5 m tall with 123 storeys above ground; a reinforced-concrete core and eight mega-columns carry gravity and lateral load, two outrigger levels and several belt trusses tie the columns to the core and transfer the diagrid lantern and hotel columns onto the mega-columns. It stands on a 6.5 m thick mat, with ground-reinforcing piles, not connected to the mat, improving fault zones. The course follows gravity sharing, outriggers, mega-column slenderness, delayed locking of belt trusses, a single-pour mat, camber, monitoring and long-term creep to unpack Korea's tallest building.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-supertall","subcategoryTitle":"超高層建築巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"Supertall building landmarks","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-supertall","learningTags":["structures","st-supertall","tower"],"architectureFamily":"tower","architectureNodes":[["鋼筋混凝土核心筒","Reinforced-concrete core"],["八根混凝土巨柱","Eight concrete mega-columns"],["外伸臂與帶狀桁架","Outriggers and belt trusses"],["頂部斜交網格燈籠","Diagrid lantern"],["6.5 m 筏基與補強樁","6.5 m mat and reinforcing piles"],["結構健康監測","Structural health monitoring"]],"architectureEdges":[[3,2],[2,1],[2,0],[0,4],[1,4],[5,0],[5,4]],"diagram":{"type":"tower","labels":["鋼筋混凝土核心筒","八根混凝土巨柱","外伸臂與帶狀桁架","頂部斜交網格燈籠","6.5 m 筏基與補強樁"],"labelsEn":["Reinforced-concrete core","Eight concrete mega-columns","Outriggers and belt trusses","Diagrid lantern","6.5 m mat and reinforcing piles"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"設計練習：檢核筏基在重力加風力下的接觸壓力。塔樓垂直荷重約 75 萬公噸，W = 750,000×9.81 ≈ 7.36×10⁶ kN；筏基 72 m×72 m，A = 5,184 m²，平均接觸壓力 q = 7.36×10⁶/5,184 ≈ 1,419 kPa。設計風傾覆力矩取 M = 2.5×10⁷ kN·m，斷面模數 S = B³/6 = 72³/6 = 62,208 m³，壓力變化 ΔM/S ≈ 402 kPa，故 q_max ≈ 1,821 kPa、q_min ≈ 1,017 kPa，與容許承壓 3,000 kPa 相比利用率約 61%；偏心 e = M/W ≈ 3.4 m 小於 B/6 = 12 m，筏基全面受壓。若 M 加倍為 5.0×10⁷ kN·m，q_max ≈ 2,223 kPa、q_min ≈ 616 kPa，利用率約 74%，e ≈ 6.8 m 仍小於 12 m。荷重與筏基尺寸取自公開資料的約略值，風力矩與承壓判讀為教學假設，不代表實際設計。","textEn":"Design exercise: check mat contact pressure under gravity plus wind. The tower's vertical load is about 750,000 t, so W = 750,000×9.81 ≈ 7.36×10⁶ kN; the mat is 72 m×72 m, A = 5,184 m², giving an average contact pressure q = 7.36×10⁶/5,184 ≈ 1,419 kPa. Take a design wind overturning moment M = 2.5×10⁷ kN·m; the section modulus is S = B³/6 = 72³/6 = 62,208 m³, so the pressure change is M/S ≈ 402 kPa, q_max ≈ 1,821 kPa and q_min ≈ 1,017 kPa, a utilisation of about 61% of the 3,000 kPa allowable; the eccentricity e = M/W ≈ 3.4 m is below B/6 = 12 m, so the whole mat stays in compression. If M doubles to 5.0×10⁷ kN·m, q_max ≈ 2,223 kPa and q_min ≈ 616 kPa, utilisation about 74%, and e ≈ 6.8 m is still below 12 m. Load and mat size are approximate public values; the wind moment and bearing interpretation are teaching assumptions, not the actual design.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b027-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔」與「外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns\" and \"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b027-v13-01","title":"核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「核心筒與八根巨柱」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Core and eight mega-columns” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"公開資料指出核心筒承擔塔樓約 60% 的重力、八根巨柱約 40%。塔身由下而上收分，核心牆在中段三分之一向內傾斜，周邊柱在兩個方向上傾斜，因此重力不只產生垂直壓力，也在樓板與帶狀桁架處產生需要被平衡的水平分力。分擔比例取決於核心牆與巨柱的相對軸向勁度與施工順序，而不是單純依樓板面積的受載區域劃分；兩者應力水準若差太多，長期潛變就會造成明顯的差異縮短。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「核心筒與八根巨柱」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Public sources state that the core carries about 60% of the tower's gravity load and the eight mega-columns about 40%. The tower tapers with height, the core walls slope inward through the middle third and the perimeter columns slope in two directions, so gravity produces horizontal components that floors and belt trusses must balance as well as vertical compression. The split depends on the relative axial stiffness of walls and columns and on the construction sequence, not simply on tributary floor areas; if their stress levels differ greatly, long-term creep produces significant differential shortening. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Core and eight mega-columns” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：設底層總重力 G = 6.0×10⁶ kN：核心筒 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN，八根巨柱共 2.4×10⁶ kN，每根約 300,000 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Take a total ground-level gravity load G = 6.0×10⁶ kN: the core carries 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN and the eight mega-columns 2.4×10⁶ kN, about 300,000 kN each.","failure":"常見誤解：「核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「核心筒與八根巨柱」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Core and eight mega-columns”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-01-k1","title":"核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔","titleEn":"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns","text":"公開資料指出核心筒承擔塔樓約 60% 的重力、八根巨柱約 40%。塔身由下而上收分，核心牆在中段三分之一向內傾斜，周邊柱在兩個方向上傾斜，因此重力不只產生垂直壓力，也在樓板與帶狀桁架處產生需要被平衡的水平分力。","textEn":"Public sources state that the core carries about 60% of the tower's gravity load and the eight mega-columns about 40%. The tower tapers with height, the core walls slope inward through the middle third and the perimeter columns slope in two directions, so gravity produces horizontal components that floors and belt trusses must balance as well as vertical compression.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns\" is correct?","options":["核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。","公開資料指出核心筒承擔塔樓約 60% 的重力、八根巨柱約 40%。","外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas.","Public sources state that the core carries about 60% of the tower's gravity load and the eight mega-columns about 40%.","More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"公開資料指出核心筒承擔塔樓約 60% 的重力、八根巨柱約 40%。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Public sources state that the core carries about 60% of the tower's gravity load and the eight mega-columns about 40%. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b027-v13-02","title":"核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔：定量估算","titleEn":"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「核心筒與八根巨柱」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Core and eight mega-columns” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：設底層總重力 G = 6.0×10⁶ kN：核心筒 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN，八根巨柱共 2.4×10⁶ kN，每根約 300,000 kN。3.3 m×3.3 m 巨柱 A = 10.89 m²，平均壓應力 σ = 300,000/10.89 ≈ 27.5 MPa，約為 80 MPa 混凝土的 34%。數值為教學假設，忽略鋼筋與鋼骨貢獻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Take a total ground-level gravity load G = 6.0×10⁶ kN: the core carries 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN and the eight mega-columns 2.4×10⁶ kN, about 300,000 kN each. A 3.3 m×3.3 m mega-column has A = 10.89 m², so the average stress σ = 300,000/10.89 ≈ 27.5 MPa, about 34% of 80 MPa concrete. Values are teaching assumptions ignoring reinforcement and embedded steel. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以施工階段分析比較一次加載與逐層加載的核心筒／巨柱分擔比，確認兩者的長期應力差落在可控制的範圍；施工中於巨柱與核心牆埋設應變計，追蹤實測應力比是否與預測的 60/40 分擔一致。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare core/mega-column load sharing from one-step loading and from storey-by-storey construction-stage analysis, confirming that their long-term stress difference is controllable; during construction embed strain gauges in mega-columns and core walls to check that the measured stress ratio follows the predicted 60/40 split.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"設底層總重力 G = 6.0×10⁶ kN：核心筒 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN，八根巨柱共 2.4×10⁶ kN，每根約 300,000 kN。3.3 m×3.3 m 巨柱 A = 10.89 m²，平均壓應力 σ = 300,000/10.89 ≈ 27.5 MPa，約為 80 MPa 混凝土的 34%。數值為教學假設，忽略鋼筋與鋼骨貢獻。","textEn":"Take a total ground-level gravity load G = 6.0×10⁶ kN: the core carries 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN and the eight mega-columns 2.4×10⁶ kN, about 300,000 kN each. A 3.3 m×3.3 m mega-column has A = 10.89 m², so the average stress σ = 300,000/10.89 ≈ 27.5 MPa, about 34% of 80 MPa concrete. Values are teaching assumptions ignoring reinforcement and embedded steel.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns\", which statement holds?","options":["延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。","筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。","設底層總重力 G = 6.0×10⁶ kN：核心筒 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN，八根巨柱共 2.4×10⁶ kN，每根約 300,000 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect.","A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.","Take a total ground-level gravity load G = 6.0×10⁶ kN: the core carries 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN and the eight mega-columns 2.4×10⁶ kN, about 300,000 kN each."],"answer":2,"explanation":"設底層總重力 G = 6.0×10⁶ kN：核心筒 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN，八根巨柱共 2.4×10⁶ kN，每根約 300,000 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Take a total ground-level gravity load G = 6.0×10⁶ kN: the core carries 0.6G = 3.6×10⁶ kN and the eight mega-columns 2.4×10⁶ kN, about 300,000 kN each. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b027-v13-03","title":"核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「核心筒與八根巨柱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Core and eight mega-columns” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以施工階段分析比較一次加載與逐層加載的核心筒／巨柱分擔比，確認兩者的長期應力差落在可控制的範圍；施工中於巨柱與核心牆埋設應變計，追蹤實測應力比是否與預測的 60/40 分擔一致。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare core/mega-column load sharing from one-step loading and from storey-by-storey construction-stage analysis, confirming that their long-term stress difference is controllable; during construction embed strain gauges in mega-columns and core walls to check that the measured stress ratio follows the predicted 60/40 split. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：設計初期就把核心牆與巨柱的長期應力差列為設計目標之一，必要時調整巨柱斷面或混凝土強度讓兩者應力相近，並在設計基準中寫明預期分擔比與監測驗證方式。","observationEn":"Site practice: Treat the long-term stress difference between core walls and mega-columns as a design target from the outset, adjusting column size or concrete strength to bring stresses closer, and state the expected load split and its monitoring verification in the design basis.","failure":"注意干擾：若巨柱應力遠高於核心牆，巨柱的彈性與潛變縮短會比核心筒大，周邊樓板逐年向外傾斜，連接兩者的樓板梁與外伸臂鎖入額外力量；反之核心筒縮短較多時，電梯與管道井的垂直度也會受影響。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If mega-column stresses are much higher than core-wall stresses, the columns shorten more elastically and by creep, perimeter floors tilt outward year by year and the beams and outriggers between them lock in extra forces; if the core shortens more, elevator and riser verticality suffers. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以施工階段分析比較一次加載與逐層加載的核心筒／巨柱分擔比，確認兩者的長期應力差落在可控制的範圍；施工中於巨柱與核心牆埋設應變計，追蹤實測應力比是否與預測的 60/40 分擔一致。","textEn":"Compare core/mega-column load sharing from one-step loading and from storey-by-storey construction-stage analysis, confirming that their long-term stress difference is controllable; during construction embed strain gauges in mega-columns and core walls to check that the measured stress ratio follows the predicted 60/40 split.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"設計初期就把核心牆與巨柱的長期應力差列為設計目標之一，必要時調整巨柱斷面或混凝土強度讓兩者應力相近，並在設計基準中寫明預期分擔比與監測驗證方式。","textEn":"Treat the long-term stress difference between core walls and mega-columns as a design target from the outset, adjusting column size or concrete strength to bring stresses closer, and state the expected load split and its monitoring verification in the design basis.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns\"?","options":["以施工階段分析比較一次加載與逐層加載的核心筒／巨柱分擔比，確認兩者的長期應力差落在可控制的範圍。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。"],"optionsEn":["Compare core/mega-column load sharing from one-step loading and from storey-by-storey construction-stage analysis, confirming that their long-term stress difference is controllable.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以施工階段分析比較一次加載與逐層加載的核心筒／巨柱分擔比，確認兩者的長期應力差落在可控制的範圍；施工中於巨柱與核心牆埋設應變計，追蹤實測應力比是否與預測的 60/40 分擔一致。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare core/mega-column load sharing from one-step loading and from storey-by-storey construction-stage analysis, confirming that their long-term stress difference is controllable; during construction embed strain gauges in mega-columns and core walls to check that the measured stress ratio follows the predicted 60/40 split. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b027-v13-04","title":"核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔：失效診斷","titleEn":"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「核心筒與八根巨柱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Core and eight mega-columns” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若巨柱應力遠高於核心牆，巨柱的彈性與潛變縮短會比核心筒大，周邊樓板逐年向外傾斜，連接兩者的樓板梁與外伸臂鎖入額外力量；反之核心筒縮短較多時，電梯與管道井的垂直度也會受影響。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If mega-column stresses are much higher than core-wall stresses, the columns shorten more elastically and by creep, perimeter floors tilt outward year by year and the beams and outriggers between them lock in extra forces; if the core shortens more, elevator and riser verticality suffers. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：分擔比例取決於核心牆與巨柱的相對軸向勁度與施工順序，而不是單純依樓板面積的受載區域劃分；兩者應力水準若差太多，長期潛變就會造成明顯的差異縮短。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The split depends on the relative axial stiffness of walls and columns and on the construction sequence, not simply on tributary floor areas; if their stress levels differ greatly, long-term creep produces significant differential shortening.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若巨柱應力遠高於核心牆，巨柱的彈性與潛變縮短會比核心筒大，周邊樓板逐年向外傾斜，連接兩者的樓板梁與外伸臂鎖入額外力量；反之核心筒縮短較多時，電梯與管道井的垂直度也會受影響。","textEn":"If mega-column stresses are much higher than core-wall stresses, the columns shorten more elastically and by creep, perimeter floors tilt outward year by year and the beams and outriggers between them lock in extra forces; if the core shortens more, elevator and riser verticality suffers.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Gravity sharing between core and mega-columns\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若巨柱應力遠高於核心牆，巨柱的彈性與潛變縮短會比核心筒大，周邊樓板逐年向外傾斜，連接兩者的樓板梁與外伸臂鎖入額外力量。","外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If mega-column stresses are much higher than core-wall stresses, the columns shorten more elastically and by creep, perimeter floors tilt outward year by year and the beams and outriggers between them lock in extra forces.","More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若巨柱應力遠高於核心牆，巨柱的彈性與潛變縮短會比核心筒大，周邊樓板逐年向外傾斜，連接兩者的樓板梁與外伸臂鎖入額外力量；反之核心筒縮短較多時，電梯與管道井的垂直度也會受影響。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If mega-column stresses are much higher than core-wall stresses, the columns shorten more elastically and by creep, perimeter floors tilt outward year by year and the beams and outriggers between them lock in extra forces; if the core shortens more, elevator and riser verticality suffers. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b027-v13-05","title":"外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「兩道外伸臂與帶狀桁架」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Two outrigger levels and belt trusses” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外伸臂位於約 39–44 層與 72–76 層的機械避難層，帶狀桁架位於約 72–76 層與 104–107 層。當核心筒在風或地震下彎曲旋轉，外伸臂迫使一側巨柱受拉減壓、另一側受壓，形成反向力偶抵消部分核心彎矩，頂部變位與加速度隨之下降；帶狀桁架則把周邊柱串成整圈，使非直接連到外伸臂的柱也參與作用，同時把頂部燈籠與飯店層的柱轉換到巨柱上。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「兩道外伸臂與帶狀桁架」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Outriggers sit at mechanical and refuge levels around floors 39–44 and 72–76, and belt trusses around floors 72–76 and 104–107. When the core bends and rotates under wind or earthquake, the outriggers force mega-columns on one side into tension relief and on the other into extra compression, creating a restoring couple that cancels part of the core moment and reduces top drift and acceleration; the belt trusses tie the perimeter into a ring so columns not directly attached to an outrigger also participate, while transferring the lantern and hotel columns onto the mega-columns. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Two outrigger levels and belt trusses” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：外伸臂恢復力矩 M_o = ΔP·d。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The outrigger restoring moment is M_o = ΔP·d.","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「兩道外伸臂與帶狀桁架」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Two outrigger levels and belt trusses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-05-k1","title":"外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用","titleEn":"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses","text":"外伸臂位於約 39–44 層與 72–76 層的機械避難層，帶狀桁架位於約 72–76 層與 104–107 層。當核心筒在風或地震下彎曲旋轉，外伸臂迫使一側巨柱受拉減壓、另一側受壓，形成反向力偶抵消部分核心彎矩，頂部變位與加速度隨之下降；帶狀桁架則把周邊柱串成整圈，使非直接連到外伸臂的柱也參與作用，同時把頂部燈籠與飯店層的柱轉換到巨柱上。","textEn":"Outriggers sit at mechanical and refuge levels around floors 39–44 and 72–76, and belt trusses around floors 72–76 and 104–107. When the core bends and rotates under wind or earthquake, the outriggers force mega-columns on one side into tension relief and on the other into extra compression, creating a restoring couple that cancels part of the core moment and reduces top drift and acceleration; the belt trusses tie the perimeter into a ring so columns not directly attached to an outrigger also participate, while transferring the lantern and hotel columns onto the mega-columns.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。","巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。","外伸臂位於約 39–44 層與 72–76 層的機械避難層，帶狀桁架位於約 72–76 層與 104–107 層。"],"optionsEn":["More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better.","A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues.","Outriggers sit at mechanical and refuge levels around floors 39–44 and 72–76, and belt trusses around floors 72–76 and 104–107."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外伸臂位於約 39–44 層與 72–76 層的機械避難層，帶狀桁架位於約 72–76 層與 104–107 層。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Outriggers sit at mechanical and refuge levels around floors 39–44 and 72–76, and belt trusses around floors 72–76 and 104–107. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b027-v13-06","title":"外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用：定量估算","titleEn":"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「兩道外伸臂與帶狀桁架」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Two outrigger levels and belt trusses” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：外伸臂恢復力矩 M_o = ΔP·d。若一側巨柱群產生 ΔP = 50,000 kN 的軸力變化、兩側力臂 d = 50 m，M_o = 50,000×50 = 2.5×10⁶ kN·m；若該高度以下核心筒承受的風彎矩為 1.0×10⁷ kN·m，外伸臂約抵消 25%。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The outrigger restoring moment is M_o = ΔP·d. If the mega-column group on one side changes axial force by ΔP = 50,000 kN with a lever arm d = 50 m between sides, M_o = 50,000×50 = 2.5×10⁶ kN·m; against a core wind moment of 1.0×10⁷ kN·m below that level, the outriggers relieve about 25%. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在分析模型中逐一移除各外伸臂層，比較頂部變位、加速度與核心筒基座力矩，確認每道外伸臂的效益；並核對外伸臂斜桿與巨柱接頭在風、地震及長期差異縮短組合下的設計力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Remove each outrigger level in turn in the analysis model and compare top drift, acceleration and core base moment to confirm each level's benefit; check the design forces in outrigger diagonals and mega-column connections under wind, earthquake and long-term differential shortening combinations.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"外伸臂恢復力矩 M_o = ΔP·d。若一側巨柱群產生 ΔP = 50,000 kN 的軸力變化、兩側力臂 d = 50 m，M_o = 50,000×50 = 2.5×10⁶ kN·m；若該高度以下核心筒承受的風彎矩為 1.0×10⁷ kN·m，外伸臂約抵消 25%。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The outrigger restoring moment is M_o = ΔP·d. If the mega-column group on one side changes axial force by ΔP = 50,000 kN with a lever arm d = 50 m between sides, M_o = 50,000×50 = 2.5×10⁶ kN·m; against a core wind moment of 1.0×10⁷ kN·m below that level, the outriggers relieve about 25%. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸臂恢復力矩 M_o = ΔP·d。","巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。","完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。"],"optionsEn":["The outrigger restoring moment is M_o = ΔP·d.","If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference.","A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外伸臂恢復力矩 M_o = ΔP·d。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The outrigger restoring moment is M_o = ΔP·d. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b027-v13-07","title":"外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「兩道外伸臂與帶狀桁架」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Two outrigger levels and belt trusses” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在分析模型中逐一移除各外伸臂層，比較頂部變位、加速度與核心筒基座力矩，確認每道外伸臂的效益；並核對外伸臂斜桿與巨柱接頭在風、地震及長期差異縮短組合下的設計力。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Remove each outrigger level in turn in the analysis model and compare top drift, acceleration and core base moment to confirm each level's benefit; check the design forces in outrigger diagonals and mega-column connections under wind, earthquake and long-term differential shortening combinations. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：外伸臂層位置要與建築的機械、避難與空中大廳樓層共同決定，並在合約文件中規定外伸臂最終接合的時機與調整機制；每道外伸臂都應有可追溯的設計力來源說明。","observationEn":"Site practice: Decide outrigger levels together with the mechanical, refuge and sky-lobby floors, specify in the contract documents when and how outriggers are finally connected, and document the source of every outrigger design force.","failure":"注意干擾：外伸臂太剛時，巨柱與核心筒的差異縮短會在斜桿與接頭中鎖入巨大附加力，甚至超過風荷載本身；外伸臂太柔或位置不當，則無法有效降低變位，只增加機械層的鋼量與施工難度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Outriggers that are too stiff lock large additional forces from differential shortening into diagonals and joints, sometimes exceeding the wind forces themselves; outriggers that are too flexible or poorly placed fail to reduce drift and only add steel and complexity to mechanical floors. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在分析模型中逐一移除各外伸臂層，比較頂部變位、加速度與核心筒基座力矩，確認每道外伸臂的效益；並核對外伸臂斜桿與巨柱接頭在風、地震及長期差異縮短組合下的設計力。","textEn":"Remove each outrigger level in turn in the analysis model and compare top drift, acceleration and core base moment to confirm each level's benefit; check the design forces in outrigger diagonals and mega-column connections under wind, earthquake and long-term differential shortening combinations.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"外伸臂層位置要與建築的機械、避難與空中大廳樓層共同決定，並在合約文件中規定外伸臂最終接合的時機與調整機制；每道外伸臂都應有可追溯的設計力來源說明。","textEn":"Decide outrigger levels together with the mechanical, refuge and sky-lobby floors, specify in the contract documents when and how outriggers are finally connected, and document the source of every outrigger design force.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在分析模型中逐一移除各外伸臂層，比較頂部變位、加速度與核心筒基座力矩，確認每道外伸臂的效益；並核對外伸臂斜桿與巨柱接頭在風、地震及長期差異縮短組合下的設計力。","外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Remove each outrigger level in turn in the analysis model and compare top drift, acceleration and core base moment to confirm each level's benefit.","Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在分析模型中逐一移除各外伸臂層，比較頂部變位、加速度與核心筒基座力矩，確認每道外伸臂的效益；並核對外伸臂斜桿與巨柱接頭在風、地震及長期差異縮短組合下的設計力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Remove each outrigger level in turn in the analysis model and compare top drift, acceleration and core base moment to confirm each level's benefit; check the design forces in outrigger diagonals and mega-column connections under wind, earthquake and long-term differential shortening combinations. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b027-v13-08","title":"外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用：失效診斷","titleEn":"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「兩道外伸臂與帶狀桁架」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Two outrigger levels and belt trusses” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"外伸臂太剛時，巨柱與核心筒的差異縮短會在斜桿與接頭中鎖入巨大附加力，甚至超過風荷載本身；外伸臂太柔或位置不當，則無法有效降低變位，只增加機械層的鋼量與施工難度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Outriggers that are too stiff lock large additional forces from differential shortening into diagonals and joints, sometimes exceeding the wind forces themselves; outriggers that are too flexible or poorly placed fail to reduce drift and only add steel and complexity to mechanical floors. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：當核心筒在風或地震下彎曲旋轉，外伸臂迫使一側巨柱受拉減壓、另一側受壓，形成反向力偶抵消部分核心彎矩，頂部變位與加速度隨之下降；帶狀桁架則把周邊柱串成整圈，使非直接連到外伸臂的柱也參與作用，同時把頂部燈籠與飯店層的柱轉換到巨柱上。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: When the core bends and rotates under wind or earthquake, the outriggers force mega-columns on one side into tension relief and on the other into extra compression, creating a restoring couple that cancels part of the core moment and reduces top drift and acceleration; the belt trusses tie the perimeter into a ring so columns not directly attached to an outrigger also participate, while transferring the lantern and hotel columns onto the mega-columns.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"外伸臂太剛時，巨柱與核心筒的差異縮短會在斜桿與接頭中鎖入巨大附加力，甚至超過風荷載本身；外伸臂太柔或位置不當，則無法有效降低變位，只增加機械層的鋼量與施工難度。","textEn":"Outriggers that are too stiff lock large additional forces from differential shortening into diagonals and joints, sometimes exceeding the wind forces themselves; outriggers that are too flexible or poorly placed fail to reduce drift and only add steel and complexity to mechanical floors.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「外伸臂與帶狀桁架的側向作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Lateral action of outriggers and belt trusses\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。","外伸臂太剛時，巨柱與核心筒的差異縮短會在斜桿與接頭中鎖入巨大附加力，甚至超過風荷載本身；外伸臂太柔或位置不當，則無法有效降低變位，只增加機械層的鋼量與施工難度。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues.","Outriggers that are too stiff lock large additional forces from differential shortening into diagonals and joints, sometimes exceeding the wind forces themselves."],"answer":2,"explanation":"外伸臂太剛時，巨柱與核心筒的差異縮短會在斜桿與接頭中鎖入巨大附加力，甚至超過風荷載本身；外伸臂太柔或位置不當，則無法有效降低變位，只增加機械層的鋼量與施工難度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Outriggers that are too stiff lock large additional forces from differential shortening into diagonals and joints, sometimes exceeding the wind forces themselves; outriggers that are too flexible or poorly placed fail to reduce drift and only add steel and complexity to mechanical floors. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b027-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應」與「帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness\" and \"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b027-v13-09","title":"巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「3.3 m 巨柱細長效應」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “3.3 m mega-column slenderness” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"巨柱由地面約 3.3 m 見方逐段縮小到約 1.4 m×2.3 m，核心牆與巨柱混凝土強度約 40 至 80 MPa。設計者指出底部巨柱在前八層沒有樓板側撐，屬細長構件：無側撐長度大時，軸力會放大柱身的初始彎矩與偏心，二階效應使彎矩比一階分析大得多。巨柱斷面逐段縮小時，偏心與勁度突變處也要特別檢核，避免應力集中與鋼筋續接過度擁擠。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「3.3 m 巨柱細長效應」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The mega-columns step down from about 3.3 m square at ground to about 1.4 m×2.3 m higher up, and core and column concrete ranges from about 40 to 80 MPa. The designers note that the base mega-columns are unbraced by floors for the first eight levels and qualify as slender members: over a long unbraced length the axial load magnifies initial bending and eccentricity, so second-order moments are much larger than first-order analysis suggests. Where the section steps down, eccentricities and abrupt stiffness changes need specific checks to avoid stress concentrations and congested bar splices. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “3.3 m mega-column slenderness” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa，I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴，有效 EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m²。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa, I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴ and an effective EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m².","failure":"常見誤解：「巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「3.3 m 巨柱細長效應」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “3.3 m mega-column slenderness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-09-k1","title":"巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應","titleEn":"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness","text":"巨柱由地面約 3.3 m 見方逐段縮小到約 1.4 m×2.3 m，核心牆與巨柱混凝土強度約 40 至 80 MPa。設計者指出底部巨柱在前八層沒有樓板側撐，屬細長構件：無側撐長度大時，軸力會放大柱身的初始彎矩與偏心，二階效應使彎矩比一階分析大得多。","textEn":"The mega-columns step down from about 3.3 m square at ground to about 1.4 m×2.3 m higher up, and core and column concrete ranges from about 40 to 80 MPa. The designers note that the base mega-columns are unbraced by floors for the first eight levels and qualify as slender members: over a long unbraced length the axial load magnifies initial bending and eccentricity, so second-order moments are much larger than first-order analysis suggests.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness\" is correct?","options":["巨柱由地面約 3.3 m 見方逐段縮小到約 1.4 m×2.3 m，核心牆與巨柱混凝土強度約 40 至 80 MPa。","巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。","延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["The mega-columns step down from about 3.3 m square at ground to about 1.4 m×2.3 m higher up, and core and column concrete ranges from about 40 to 80 MPa.","A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues.","Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"巨柱由地面約 3.3 m 見方逐段縮小到約 1.4 m×2.3 m，核心牆與巨柱混凝土強度約 40 至 80 MPa。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The mega-columns step down from about 3.3 m square at ground to about 1.4 m×2.3 m higher up, and core and column concrete ranges from about 40 to 80 MPa. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b027-v13-10","title":"巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應：定量估算","titleEn":"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「3.3 m 巨柱細長效應」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “3.3 m mega-column slenderness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa，I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴，有效 EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m²。無側撐長度 40 m 時 P_c = π²EI/L² ≈ 1.03×10⁶ kN；設計軸力 P_u = 360,000 kN，彎矩放大 δ = 1/(1 − P_u/0.75P_c) = 1/(1 − 0.468) ≈ 1.88。若長度增為 48 m，δ ≈ 3.07。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa, I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴ and an effective EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m². For a 40 m unbraced length P_c = π²EI/L² ≈ 1.03×10⁶ kN; with a design axial load P_u = 360,000 kN the moment magnifier δ = 1/(1 − P_u/0.75P_c) = 1/(1 − 0.468) ≈ 1.88. At 48 m, δ ≈ 3.07. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以考慮幾何非線性、開裂與潛變的二階分析複核巨柱彎矩，並與規範的彎矩放大法比較；施工時量測巨柱垂直度與模板偏位，確認初始偏心不超過分析假設值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check mega-column moments with second-order analysis including geometric nonlinearity, cracking and creep, and compare with the code moment-magnifier method; during construction survey column plumbness and formwork offsets to confirm that initial eccentricity stays within the analysis assumption.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa，I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴，有效 EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m²。無側撐長度 40 m 時 P_c = π²EI/L² ≈ 1.03×10⁶ kN；設計軸力 P_u = 360,000 kN，彎矩放大 δ = 1/(1 − P_u/0.75P_c) = 1/(1 − 0.468) ≈ 1.88。若長度增為 48 m，δ ≈ 3.07。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa, I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴ and an effective EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m². For a 40 m unbraced length P_c = π²EI/L² ≈ 1.03×10⁶ kN; with a design axial load P_u = 360,000 kN the moment magnifier δ = 1/(1 − P_u/0.75P_c) = 1/(1 − 0.468) ≈ 1.88. At 48 m, δ ≈ 3.07. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness\", which statement holds?","options":["筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。","E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa，I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴，有效 EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m²。","樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。"],"optionsEn":["A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.","E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa, I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴ and an effective EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m².","Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat."],"answer":1,"explanation":"E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa，I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴，有效 EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m²。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"E_c = 4,700√80 ≈ 42,040 MPa, I_g = 3.3⁴/12 ≈ 9.88 m⁴ and an effective EI = 0.4E_cI_g ≈ 1.66×10⁸ kN·m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b027-v13-11","title":"巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「3.3 m 巨柱細長效應」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “3.3 m mega-column slenderness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以考慮幾何非線性、開裂與潛變的二階分析複核巨柱彎矩，並與規範的彎矩放大法比較；施工時量測巨柱垂直度與模板偏位，確認初始偏心不超過分析假設值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check mega-column moments with second-order analysis including geometric nonlinearity, cracking and creep, and compare with the code moment-magnifier method; during construction survey column plumbness and formwork offsets to confirm that initial eccentricity stays within the analysis assumption. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：無側撐高度大的巨柱應在施工計畫中訂定垂直度允差與量測頻率，並在澆置前檢查鋼筋續接區的淨距；斷面變化層的配筋詳圖須經結構工程師複核。","observationEn":"Site practice: For mega-columns with tall unbraced heights, set plumbness tolerances and survey frequency in the construction plan and check clear spacing at splice zones before casting; reinforcement details at step-down floors must be reviewed by the structural engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：若忽略二階效應或低估施工偏位，巨柱在設計風或地震下的實際彎矩可能超出容量，柱身出現水平裂縫；斷面縮小處若續接鋼筋過密導致混凝土充填不良，也會形成弱點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring second-order effects or underestimating construction offsets can let real mega-column moments under design wind or earthquake exceed capacity, cracking the shaft horizontally; overcrowded splices at step-downs that leave poorly compacted concrete also create weak spots. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以考慮幾何非線性、開裂與潛變的二階分析複核巨柱彎矩，並與規範的彎矩放大法比較；施工時量測巨柱垂直度與模板偏位，確認初始偏心不超過分析假設值。","textEn":"Check mega-column moments with second-order analysis including geometric nonlinearity, cracking and creep, and compare with the code moment-magnifier method; during construction survey column plumbness and formwork offsets to confirm that initial eccentricity stays within the analysis assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"無側撐高度大的巨柱應在施工計畫中訂定垂直度允差與量測頻率，並在澆置前檢查鋼筋續接區的淨距；斷面變化層的配筋詳圖須經結構工程師複核。","textEn":"For mega-columns with tall unbraced heights, set plumbness tolerances and survey frequency in the construction plan and check clear spacing at splice zones before casting; reinforcement details at step-down floors must be reviewed by the structural engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。","以考慮幾何非線性、開裂與潛變的二階分析複核巨柱彎矩，並與規範的彎矩放大法比較；施工時量測巨柱垂直度與模板偏位，確認初始偏心不超過分析假設值。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance.","Check mega-column moments with second-order analysis including geometric nonlinearity, cracking and creep, and compare with the code moment-magnifier method."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以考慮幾何非線性、開裂與潛變的二階分析複核巨柱彎矩，並與規範的彎矩放大法比較；施工時量測巨柱垂直度與模板偏位，確認初始偏心不超過分析假設值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check mega-column moments with second-order analysis including geometric nonlinearity, cracking and creep, and compare with the code moment-magnifier method; during construction survey column plumbness and formwork offsets to confirm that initial eccentricity stays within the analysis assumption. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b027-v13-12","title":"巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「3.3 m 巨柱細長效應」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “3.3 m mega-column slenderness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若忽略二階效應或低估施工偏位，巨柱在設計風或地震下的實際彎矩可能超出容量，柱身出現水平裂縫；斷面縮小處若續接鋼筋過密導致混凝土充填不良，也會形成弱點。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring second-order effects or underestimating construction offsets can let real mega-column moments under design wind or earthquake exceed capacity, cracking the shaft horizontally; overcrowded splices at step-downs that leave poorly compacted concrete also create weak spots. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：巨柱斷面逐段縮小時，偏心與勁度突變處也要特別檢核，避免應力集中與鋼筋續接過度擁擠。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Where the section steps down, eccentricities and abrupt stiffness changes need specific checks to avoid stress concentrations and congested bar splices.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若忽略二階效應或低估施工偏位，巨柱在設計風或地震下的實際彎矩可能超出容量，柱身出現水平裂縫；斷面縮小處若續接鋼筋過密導致混凝土充填不良，也會形成弱點。","textEn":"Ignoring second-order effects or underestimating construction offsets can let real mega-column moments under design wind or earthquake exceed capacity, cracking the shaft horizontally; overcrowded splices at step-downs that leave poorly compacted concrete also create weak spots.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「巨柱尺寸遞減與細長效應」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mega-column step-downs and slenderness\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若忽略二階效應或低估施工偏位，巨柱在設計風或地震下的實際彎矩可能超出容量，柱身出現水平裂縫；斷面縮小處若續接鋼筋過密導致混凝土充填不良，也會形成弱點。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring second-order effects or underestimating construction offsets can let real mega-column moments under design wind or earthquake exceed capacity, cracking the shaft horizontally.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若忽略二階效應或低估施工偏位，巨柱在設計風或地震下的實際彎矩可能超出容量，柱身出現水平裂縫；斷面縮小處若續接鋼筋過密導致混凝土充填不良，也會形成弱點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring second-order effects or underestimating construction offsets can let real mega-column moments under design wind or earthquake exceed capacity, cracking the shaft horizontally; overcrowded splices at step-downs that leave poorly compacted concrete also create weak spots. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b027-v13-13","title":"帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「帶狀桁架預埋板與長槽孔」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Belt-truss embed plates and long slots” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"帶狀桁架由預組段件在現場焊接到巨柱外側的預埋鋼板上，讓巨柱混凝土能連續施作而不被鋼構中斷。公開報導指出部分柱與帶狀桁架的接合採長槽孔，螺栓在塔樓完成後才鎖緊與重新定位；設計者也建議延後外伸臂最終接合，並設計長期力量轉移。長槽孔讓核心筒與巨柱在施工期的差異縮短自由發生，等主要重力就位後再鎖定，以減少鎖入的附加力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「帶狀桁架預埋板與長槽孔」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Belt trusses are pre-assembled in sections and field-welded to embedded steel plates on the outside of the mega-columns, so the column concrete can be cast continuously without interruption by steelwork. Published reports say some column-to-belt-truss connections used long-slotted holes, with bolts tensioned and re-indexed after the tower was completed, and the designers recommended delaying the final outrigger connections and designing for long-term force transfer. The slots let differential shortening between core and columns occur freely during construction and are locked only after most gravity load is in place, reducing locked-in forces. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Belt-truss embed plates and long slots” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：長槽孔長度 ≈ 孔徑 + 2δ。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Long-slot length ≈ hole diameter + 2δ.","failure":"常見誤解：「延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「帶狀桁架預埋板與長槽孔」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Belt-truss embed plates and long slots”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-13-k1","title":"帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定","titleEn":"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking","text":"帶狀桁架由預組段件在現場焊接到巨柱外側的預埋鋼板上，讓巨柱混凝土能連續施作而不被鋼構中斷。公開報導指出部分柱與帶狀桁架的接合採長槽孔，螺栓在塔樓完成後才鎖緊與重新定位；設計者也建議延後外伸臂最終接合，並設計長期力量轉移。","textEn":"Belt trusses are pre-assembled in sections and field-welded to embedded steel plates on the outside of the mega-columns, so the column concrete can be cast continuously without interruption by steelwork. Published reports say some column-to-belt-truss connections used long-slotted holes, with bolts tensioned and re-indexed after the tower was completed, and the designers recommended delaying the final outrigger connections and designing for long-term force transfer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking\" is correct?","options":["延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。","帶狀桁架由預組段件在現場焊接到巨柱外側的預埋鋼板上，讓巨柱混凝土能連續施作而不被鋼構中斷。","巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。"],"optionsEn":["Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect.","Belt trusses are pre-assembled in sections and field-welded to embedded steel plates on the outside of the mega-columns, so the column concrete can be cast continuously without interruption by steelwork.","If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference."],"answer":1,"explanation":"帶狀桁架由預組段件在現場焊接到巨柱外側的預埋鋼板上，讓巨柱混凝土能連續施作而不被鋼構中斷。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Belt trusses are pre-assembled in sections and field-welded to embedded steel plates on the outside of the mega-columns, so the column concrete can be cast continuously without interruption by steelwork. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b027-v13-14","title":"帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定：定量估算","titleEn":"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「帶狀桁架預埋板與長槽孔」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Belt-truss embed plates and long slots” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：長槽孔長度 ≈ 孔徑 + 2δ。M30 螺栓標準孔徑 33 mm，若鎖定前預期相對位移 δ = ±20 mm，槽長 = 33 + 2×20 = 73 mm，未超過 AISC 對 M30 長槽孔約 75 mm 的上限；若 δ = ±25 mm，需 83 mm，就必須改用其他可調細部。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Long-slot length ≈ hole diameter + 2δ. For an M30 bolt with a 33 mm standard hole and an expected movement of δ = ±20 mm before locking, the slot is 33 + 2×20 = 73 mm, within the AISC long-slot limit of about 75 mm for M30; for δ = ±25 mm it would need 83 mm, so another adjustable detail is required. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：鎖定前量測每個長槽孔內螺栓相對槽端的位置，確認尚有足夠的雙向餘裕；鎖定作業依預拉力規範抽驗，並以測量標高與應變紀錄證明鎖定時差異縮短已達預測比例。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before locking, measure each bolt's position relative to the slot ends to confirm remaining travel in both directions; sample pretension during locking to the bolting specification, and use level surveys and strain records to show that the predicted proportion of differential shortening had occurred at the time of locking.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"長槽孔長度 ≈ 孔徑 + 2δ。M30 螺栓標準孔徑 33 mm，若鎖定前預期相對位移 δ = ±20 mm，槽長 = 33 + 2×20 = 73 mm，未超過 AISC 對 M30 長槽孔約 75 mm 的上限；若 δ = ±25 mm，需 83 mm，就必須改用其他可調細部。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Long-slot length ≈ hole diameter + 2δ. For an M30 bolt with a 33 mm standard hole and an expected movement of δ = ±20 mm before locking, the slot is 33 + 2×20 = 73 mm, within the AISC long-slot limit of about 75 mm for M30; for δ = ±25 mm it would need 83 mm, so another adjustable detail is required. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking\", which statement holds?","options":["完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。","外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。","長槽孔長度 ≈ 孔徑 + 2δ。"],"optionsEn":["A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model.","Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change.","Long-slot length ≈ hole diameter + 2δ."],"answer":2,"explanation":"長槽孔長度 ≈ 孔徑 + 2δ。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Long-slot length ≈ hole diameter + 2δ. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b027-v13-15","title":"帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「帶狀桁架預埋板與長槽孔」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Belt-truss embed plates and long slots” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"鎖定前量測每個長槽孔內螺栓相對槽端的位置，確認尚有足夠的雙向餘裕；鎖定作業依預拉力規範抽驗，並以測量標高與應變紀錄證明鎖定時差異縮短已達預測比例。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before locking, measure each bolt's position relative to the slot ends to confirm remaining travel in both directions; sample pretension during locking to the bolting specification, and use level surveys and strain records to show that the predicted proportion of differential shortening had occurred at the time of locking. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：延遲接頭須在施工圖與現場以醒目標籤標示「暫不鎖定」，鎖定時機列為停留點，由結構工程師依監測資料確認後才可施作，並保存鎖定日期與預拉力紀錄。","observationEn":"Site practice: Delayed joints should be tagged as do-not-lock on drawings and on site, with locking treated as a hold point released only after the structural engineer confirms the monitoring data, and the locking date and pretension records kept.","failure":"注意干擾：若螺栓在施工中途就被誤鎖或槽孔餘裕不足，差異縮短會讓螺栓頂住槽端並剪斷或使連接板挫屈；預埋板錨筋若設計不足，現場焊接與鎖入力也可能把預埋板從巨柱拉脫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If bolts are tightened prematurely or the slots run out of travel, differential shortening drives bolts against slot ends, shearing them or buckling the plates; under-designed anchors behind embedded plates can let welding stresses and locked-in forces pull the plates out of the column. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"鎖定前量測每個長槽孔內螺栓相對槽端的位置，確認尚有足夠的雙向餘裕；鎖定作業依預拉力規範抽驗，並以測量標高與應變紀錄證明鎖定時差異縮短已達預測比例。","textEn":"Before locking, measure each bolt's position relative to the slot ends to confirm remaining travel in both directions; sample pretension during locking to the bolting specification, and use level surveys and strain records to show that the predicted proportion of differential shortening had occurred at the time of locking.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"延遲接頭須在施工圖與現場以醒目標籤標示「暫不鎖定」，鎖定時機列為停留點，由結構工程師依監測資料確認後才可施作，並保存鎖定日期與預拉力紀錄。","textEn":"Delayed joints should be tagged as do-not-lock on drawings and on site, with locking treated as a hold point released only after the structural engineer confirms the monitoring data, and the locking date and pretension records kept.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking\"?","options":["鎖定前量測每個長槽孔內螺栓相對槽端的位置，確認尚有足夠的雙向餘裕；鎖定作業依預拉力規範抽驗，並以測量標高與應變紀錄證明鎖定時差異縮短已達預測比例。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。"],"optionsEn":["Before locking, measure each bolt's position relative to the slot ends to confirm remaining travel in both directions.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鎖定前量測每個長槽孔內螺栓相對槽端的位置，確認尚有足夠的雙向餘裕；鎖定作業依預拉力規範抽驗，並以測量標高與應變紀錄證明鎖定時差異縮短已達預測比例。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before locking, measure each bolt's position relative to the slot ends to confirm remaining travel in both directions; sample pretension during locking to the bolting specification, and use level surveys and strain records to show that the predicted proportion of differential shortening had occurred at the time of locking. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b027-v13-16","title":"帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「帶狀桁架預埋板與長槽孔」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Belt-truss embed plates and long slots” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若螺栓在施工中途就被誤鎖或槽孔餘裕不足，差異縮短會讓螺栓頂住槽端並剪斷或使連接板挫屈；預埋板錨筋若設計不足，現場焊接與鎖入力也可能把預埋板從巨柱拉脫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If bolts are tightened prematurely or the slots run out of travel, differential shortening drives bolts against slot ends, shearing them or buckling the plates; under-designed anchors behind embedded plates can let welding stresses and locked-in forces pull the plates out of the column. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：長槽孔讓核心筒與巨柱在施工期的差異縮短自由發生，等主要重力就位後再鎖定，以減少鎖入的附加力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The slots let differential shortening between core and columns occur freely during construction and are locked only after most gravity load is in place, reducing locked-in forces.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若螺栓在施工中途就被誤鎖或槽孔餘裕不足，差異縮短會讓螺栓頂住槽端並剪斷或使連接板挫屈；預埋板錨筋若設計不足，現場焊接與鎖入力也可能把預埋板從巨柱拉脫。","textEn":"If bolts are tightened prematurely or the slots run out of travel, differential shortening drives bolts against slot ends, shearing them or buckling the plates; under-designed anchors behind embedded plates can let welding stresses and locked-in forces pull the plates out of the column.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「帶狀桁架接頭與延遲鎖定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Belt-truss connections and delayed locking\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若螺栓在施工中途就被誤鎖或槽孔餘裕不足，差異縮短會讓螺栓頂住槽端並剪斷或使連接板挫屈；預埋板錨筋若設計不足，現場焊接與鎖入力也可能把預埋板從巨柱拉脫。","巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","If bolts are tightened prematurely or the slots run out of travel, differential shortening drives bolts against slot ends, shearing them or buckling the plates.","If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若螺栓在施工中途就被誤鎖或槽孔餘裕不足，差異縮短會讓螺栓頂住槽端並剪斷或使連接板挫屈；預埋板錨筋若設計不足，現場焊接與鎖入力也可能把預埋板從巨柱拉脫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If bolts are tightened prematurely or the slots run out of travel, differential shortening drives bolts against slot ends, shearing them or buckling the plates; under-designed anchors behind embedded plates can let welding stresses and locked-in forces pull the plates out of the column. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b027-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置」與「差異沉陷的預拱補償」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Single continuous pour of a massive mat\" and \"Camber compensation for differential settlement\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b027-v13-17","title":"巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Single continuous pour of a massive mat: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「6.5 m 筏基連續澆置」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Continuous pour of the 6.5 m mat” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"筏基約 72 m×72 m、厚 6.5 m，開挖深度約 38 m，承載塔樓約 75 萬公噸的垂直荷重，公開報導描述其以單次連續澆置完成。為避免冷縫與過高水化熱，採用 50 MPa 的低熱高流動性混凝土。單次澆置需要同時調度大量預拌車、泵車與布料點，使每一層新混凝土在下層初凝前覆蓋，讓整塊筏基成為無冷縫的整體；同時以溫度感測器控制內外溫差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「6.5 m 筏基連續澆置」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The mat is about 72 m×72 m and 6.5 m thick, at an excavation depth of about 38 m, carrying a vertical load of about 750,000 t, and was reported as placed in a single continuous pour. To avoid cold joints and excessive heat of hydration, a 50 MPa low-heat, high-flow concrete was used. A single pour demands simultaneous dispatch of many ready-mix trucks, pumps and placing points so each new layer covers the previous one before initial set, making the mat a monolith without cold joints, while temperature sensors control the interior-to-surface difference. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Continuous pour of the 6.5 m mat” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：澆置量 V = 31,200 m³、歷時 30 h，平均供料 1,040 m³/h；每層 0.5 m 覆蓋全面積需 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³，約 2.5 h 才回到同一點，初凝時間必須明顯大於 2.5 h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A volume V = 31,200 m³ placed in 30 h means an average supply of 1,040 m³/h; covering the whole area in 0.5 m layers needs 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³ per layer, so placement returns to the same spot only after about 2.5 h and initial set must be well beyond 2.5 h.","failure":"常見誤解：「巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「6.5 m 筏基連續澆置」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Continuous pour of the 6.5 m mat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-17-k1","title":"巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置","titleEn":"Single continuous pour of a massive mat","text":"筏基約 72 m×72 m、厚 6.5 m，開挖深度約 38 m，承載塔樓約 75 萬公噸的垂直荷重，公開報導描述其以單次連續澆置完成。為避免冷縫與過高水化熱，採用 50 MPa 的低熱高流動性混凝土。","textEn":"The mat is about 72 m×72 m and 6.5 m thick, at an excavation depth of about 38 m, carrying a vertical load of about 750,000 t, and was reported as placed in a single continuous pour. To avoid cold joints and excessive heat of hydration, a 50 MPa low-heat, high-flow concrete was used.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Single continuous pour of a massive mat\" is correct?","options":["巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。","筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。","筏基約 72 m×72 m、厚 6.5 m，開挖深度約 38 m，承載塔樓約 75 萬公噸的垂直荷重，公開報導描述其以單次連續澆置完成。"],"optionsEn":["If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference.","A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.","The mat is about 72 m×72 m and 6.5 m thick, at an excavation depth of about 38 m, carrying a vertical load of about 750,000 t, and was reported as placed in a single continuous pour."],"answer":2,"explanation":"筏基約 72 m×72 m、厚 6.5 m，開挖深度約 38 m，承載塔樓約 75 萬公噸的垂直荷重，公開報導描述其以單次連續澆置完成。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The mat is about 72 m×72 m and 6.5 m thick, at an excavation depth of about 38 m, carrying a vertical load of about 750,000 t, and was reported as placed in a single continuous pour. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b027-v13-18","title":"巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置：定量估算","titleEn":"Single continuous pour of a massive mat: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「6.5 m 筏基連續澆置」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Continuous pour of the 6.5 m mat” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：澆置量 V = 31,200 m³、歷時 30 h，平均供料 1,040 m³/h；每層 0.5 m 覆蓋全面積需 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³，約 2.5 h 才回到同一點，初凝時間必須明顯大於 2.5 h。若 5,300 車次，平均每車約 5.9 m³，每小時約 177 車，即約每 20 s 一車。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A volume V = 31,200 m³ placed in 30 h means an average supply of 1,040 m³/h; covering the whole area in 0.5 m layers needs 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³ per layer, so placement returns to the same spot only after about 2.5 h and initial set must be well beyond 2.5 h. With 5,300 truckloads, each carries about 5.9 m³, about 177 trucks per hour or one every 20 s. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：澆置前做配比的絕熱溫升與凝結時間試驗、泵送試驗與交通演練；澆置中記錄每車出廠時間、坍流度與溫度，布料點依網格輪替並記錄層面覆蓋時間；之後以埋設感測器追蹤最高溫度與溫差直到降至允許值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before the pour, test adiabatic temperature rise and setting time, run pumping trials and rehearse traffic; during the pour record each truck's batch time, slump flow and temperature, rotate placing points on a grid and log layer coverage times; afterwards track peak temperature and differential with embedded sensors until they fall within limits.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"澆置量 V = 31,200 m³、歷時 30 h，平均供料 1,040 m³/h；每層 0.5 m 覆蓋全面積需 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³，約 2.5 h 才回到同一點，初凝時間必須明顯大於 2.5 h。若 5,300 車次，平均每車約 5.9 m³，每小時約 177 車，即約每 20 s 一車。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A volume V = 31,200 m³ placed in 30 h means an average supply of 1,040 m³/h; covering the whole area in 0.5 m layers needs 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³ per layer, so placement returns to the same spot only after about 2.5 h and initial set must be well beyond 2.5 h. With 5,300 truckloads, each carries about 5.9 m³, about 177 trucks per hour or one every 20 s. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Single continuous pour of a massive mat\", which statement holds?","options":["澆置量 V = 31,200 m³、歷時 30 h，平均供料 1,040 m³/h。","樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。","感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。"],"optionsEn":["A volume V = 31,200 m³ placed in 30 h means an average supply of 1,040 m³/h.","Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat.","More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"澆置量 V = 31,200 m³、歷時 30 h，平均供料 1,040 m³/h；每層 0.5 m 覆蓋全面積需 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³，約 2.5 h 才回到同一點，初凝時間必須明顯大於 2.5 h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A volume V = 31,200 m³ placed in 30 h means an average supply of 1,040 m³/h; covering the whole area in 0.5 m layers needs 72×72×0.5 = 2,592 m³ per layer, so placement returns to the same spot only after about 2.5 h and initial set must be well beyond 2.5 h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b027-v13-19","title":"巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Single continuous pour of a massive mat: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「6.5 m 筏基連續澆置」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Continuous pour of the 6.5 m mat” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"澆置前做配比的絕熱溫升與凝結時間試驗、泵送試驗與交通演練；澆置中記錄每車出廠時間、坍流度與溫度，布料點依網格輪替並記錄層面覆蓋時間；之後以埋設感測器追蹤最高溫度與溫差直到降至允許值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before the pour, test adiabatic temperature rise and setting time, run pumping trials and rehearse traffic; during the pour record each truck's batch time, slump flow and temperature, rotate placing points on a grid and log layer coverage times; afterwards track peak temperature and differential with embedded sensors until they fall within limits. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：大體積澆置須有備援拌合廠、備用泵車與交通管制計畫，並預先規劃萬一中斷時的施工縫位置與處理方式；溫控計畫與停止條件須經結構工程師核准。","observationEn":"Site practice: A mass pour needs backup batching plants, standby pumps and a traffic plan, with pre-planned emergency construction-joint locations and treatment in case of interruption; the thermal control plan and stop criteria require the structural engineer's approval.","failure":"注意干擾：若供料中斷或布料不均使某區層面暴露超過初凝，就形成冷縫，成為地下水滲漏與剪力傳遞的弱面；溫差控制失敗則會在筏基表面產生貫穿性溫度裂縫。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If supply is interrupted or placement is uneven so an area stays exposed past initial set, a cold joint forms that weakens shear transfer and admits groundwater; failed temperature control causes through-thickness thermal cracks at the mat surface. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"澆置前做配比的絕熱溫升與凝結時間試驗、泵送試驗與交通演練；澆置中記錄每車出廠時間、坍流度與溫度，布料點依網格輪替並記錄層面覆蓋時間；之後以埋設感測器追蹤最高溫度與溫差直到降至允許值。","textEn":"Before the pour, test adiabatic temperature rise and setting time, run pumping trials and rehearse traffic; during the pour record each truck's batch time, slump flow and temperature, rotate placing points on a grid and log layer coverage times; afterwards track peak temperature and differential with embedded sensors until they fall within limits.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"大體積澆置須有備援拌合廠、備用泵車與交通管制計畫，並預先規劃萬一中斷時的施工縫位置與處理方式；溫控計畫與停止條件須經結構工程師核准。","textEn":"A mass pour needs backup batching plants, standby pumps and a traffic plan, with pre-planned emergency construction-joint locations and treatment in case of interruption; the thermal control plan and stop criteria require the structural engineer's approval.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Single continuous pour of a massive mat\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","澆置前做配比的絕熱溫升與凝結時間試驗、泵送試驗與交通演練。","外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Before the pour, test adiabatic temperature rise and setting time, run pumping trials and rehearse traffic.","More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better."],"answer":1,"explanation":"澆置前做配比的絕熱溫升與凝結時間試驗、泵送試驗與交通演練；澆置中記錄每車出廠時間、坍流度與溫度，布料點依網格輪替並記錄層面覆蓋時間；之後以埋設感測器追蹤最高溫度與溫差直到降至允許值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before the pour, test adiabatic temperature rise and setting time, run pumping trials and rehearse traffic; during the pour record each truck's batch time, slump flow and temperature, rotate placing points on a grid and log layer coverage times; afterwards track peak temperature and differential with embedded sensors until they fall within limits. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b027-v13-20","title":"巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置：失效診斷","titleEn":"Single continuous pour of a massive mat: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「6.5 m 筏基連續澆置」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Continuous pour of the 6.5 m mat” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若供料中斷或布料不均使某區層面暴露超過初凝，就形成冷縫，成為地下水滲漏與剪力傳遞的弱面；溫差控制失敗則會在筏基表面產生貫穿性溫度裂縫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If supply is interrupted or placement is uneven so an area stays exposed past initial set, a cold joint forms that weakens shear transfer and admits groundwater; failed temperature control causes through-thickness thermal cracks at the mat surface. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單次澆置需要同時調度大量預拌車、泵車與布料點，使每一層新混凝土在下層初凝前覆蓋，讓整塊筏基成為無冷縫的整體；同時以溫度感測器控制內外溫差。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A single pour demands simultaneous dispatch of many ready-mix trucks, pumps and placing points so each new layer covers the previous one before initial set, making the mat a monolith without cold joints, while temperature sensors control the interior-to-surface difference.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若供料中斷或布料不均使某區層面暴露超過初凝，就形成冷縫，成為地下水滲漏與剪力傳遞的弱面；溫差控制失敗則會在筏基表面產生貫穿性溫度裂縫。","textEn":"If supply is interrupted or placement is uneven so an area stays exposed past initial set, a cold joint forms that weakens shear transfer and admits groundwater; failed temperature control causes through-thickness thermal cracks at the mat surface.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「巨厚筏基的一次連續澆置」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Single continuous pour of a massive mat\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。","若供料中斷或布料不均使某區層面暴露超過初凝，就形成冷縫，成為地下水滲漏與剪力傳遞的弱面；溫差控制失敗則會在筏基表面產生貫穿性溫度裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.","If supply is interrupted or placement is uneven so an area stays exposed past initial set, a cold joint forms that weakens shear transfer and admits groundwater."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若供料中斷或布料不均使某區層面暴露超過初凝，就形成冷縫，成為地下水滲漏與剪力傳遞的弱面；溫差控制失敗則會在筏基表面產生貫穿性溫度裂縫。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If supply is interrupted or placement is uneven so an area stays exposed past initial set, a cold joint forms that weakens shear transfer and admits groundwater; failed temperature control causes through-thickness thermal cracks at the mat surface. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b027-v13-21","title":"差異沉陷的預拱補償：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Camber compensation for differential settlement: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「巨柱垂直預拱」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vertical camber of mega-columns” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"核心筒與周邊巨柱的荷重與基底剛度不同，筏基在兩者之下的沉陷量也不同。設計者以在施工中對巨柱做垂直預拱（預先抬高）的方式處理核心筒與周邊之間的差異沉陷，使完工後樓板接近水平。預拱量來自地盤—筏基互制分析與施工順序，並在施工中依實測沉陷修正；若不預拱，周邊樓板會相對核心筒下傾，影響樓板排水、帷幕牆接縫與電梯門檻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「巨柱垂直預拱」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Because the core and perimeter mega-columns carry different loads and the mat stiffness beneath them differs, the mat settles differently under each. The designers handled differential settlement between the core and perimeter by vertically cambering, or pre-raising, the mega-columns during construction so floors end up close to level. The camber comes from soil–mat interaction analysis and the construction sequence and is updated with measured settlements; without it, perimeter floors would slope down relative to the core, affecting floor drainage, façade joints and elevator sills. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Vertical camber of mega-columns” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若預測核心筒與巨柱間差異沉陷 15 mm、水平距離 20 m，角變量 = 15/20,000 = 1/1,333；對巨柱預抬 15 mm 後若殘餘誤差 ±5 mm，角變量降為 5/20,000 = 1/4,000。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If the predicted differential settlement between core and mega-column is 15 mm over 20 m, the angular distortion is 15/20,000 = 1/1,333; pre-raising the column by 15 mm with a residual error of ±5 mm reduces it to 5/20,000 = 1/4,000.","failure":"常見誤解：「筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「巨柱垂直預拱」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Vertical camber of mega-columns”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-21-k1","title":"差異沉陷的預拱補償","titleEn":"Camber compensation for differential settlement","text":"核心筒與周邊巨柱的荷重與基底剛度不同，筏基在兩者之下的沉陷量也不同。設計者以在施工中對巨柱做垂直預拱（預先抬高）的方式處理核心筒與周邊之間的差異沉陷，使完工後樓板接近水平。","textEn":"Because the core and perimeter mega-columns carry different loads and the mat stiffness beneath them differs, the mat settles differently under each. The designers handled differential settlement between the core and perimeter by vertically cambering, or pre-raising, the mega-columns during construction so floors end up close to level.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「差異沉陷的預拱補償」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Camber compensation for differential settlement\" is correct?","options":["核心筒與周邊巨柱的荷重與基底剛度不同，筏基在兩者之下的沉陷量也不同。","筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。","完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。"],"optionsEn":["Because the core and perimeter mega-columns carry different loads and the mat stiffness beneath them differs, the mat settles differently under each.","A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.","A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核心筒與周邊巨柱的荷重與基底剛度不同，筏基在兩者之下的沉陷量也不同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Because the core and perimeter mega-columns carry different loads and the mat stiffness beneath them differs, the mat settles differently under each. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b027-v13-22","title":"差異沉陷的預拱補償：定量估算","titleEn":"Camber compensation for differential settlement: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「巨柱垂直預拱」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vertical camber of mega-columns” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若預測核心筒與巨柱間差異沉陷 15 mm、水平距離 20 m，角變量 = 15/20,000 = 1/1,333；對巨柱預抬 15 mm 後若殘餘誤差 ±5 mm，角變量降為 5/20,000 = 1/4,000。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If the predicted differential settlement between core and mega-column is 15 mm over 20 m, the angular distortion is 15/20,000 = 1/1,333; pre-raising the column by 15 mm with a residual error of ±5 mm reduces it to 5/20,000 = 1/4,000. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在筏基頂面與核心筒、巨柱腳設置沉陷觀測點，每增加若干樓層量測一次，與預測曲線比較並修正後續樓層的預拱值；完工後以全樓層標高測量確認樓板平整度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Install settlement points on the mat top, core and mega-column bases, survey them after every few storeys, compare with the predicted curve and adjust camber for later floors; after completion confirm floor levelness with a full-height level survey.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若預測核心筒與巨柱間差異沉陷 15 mm、水平距離 20 m，角變量 = 15/20,000 = 1/1,333；對巨柱預抬 15 mm 後若殘餘誤差 ±5 mm，角變量降為 5/20,000 = 1/4,000。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"If the predicted differential settlement between core and mega-column is 15 mm over 20 m, the angular distortion is 15/20,000 = 1/1,333; pre-raising the column by 15 mm with a residual error of ±5 mm reduces it to 5/20,000 = 1/4,000. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「差異沉陷的預拱補償」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Camber compensation for differential settlement\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。","若預測核心筒與巨柱間差異沉陷 15 mm、水平距離 20 m，角變量 = 15/20,000 = 1/1,333。","核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。"],"optionsEn":["Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change.","If the predicted differential settlement between core and mega-column is 15 mm over 20 m, the angular distortion is 15/20,000 = 1/1,333.","The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若預測核心筒與巨柱間差異沉陷 15 mm、水平距離 20 m，角變量 = 15/20,000 = 1/1,333；對巨柱預抬 15 mm 後若殘餘誤差 ±5 mm，角變量降為 5/20,000 = 1/4,000。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If the predicted differential settlement between core and mega-column is 15 mm over 20 m, the angular distortion is 15/20,000 = 1/1,333; pre-raising the column by 15 mm with a residual error of ±5 mm reduces it to 5/20,000 = 1/4,000. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b027-v13-23","title":"差異沉陷的預拱補償：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Camber compensation for differential settlement: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「巨柱垂直預拱」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vertical camber of mega-columns” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在筏基頂面與核心筒、巨柱腳設置沉陷觀測點，每增加若干樓層量測一次，與預測曲線比較並修正後續樓層的預拱值；完工後以全樓層標高測量確認樓板平整度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Install settlement points on the mat top, core and mega-column bases, survey them after every few storeys, compare with the predicted curve and adjust camber for later floors; after completion confirm floor levelness with a full-height level survey. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：預拱值應以表格逐層列出並標註版本，每次依監測更新時由結構工程師發布新版，測量團隊只依最新版放樣，避免多版本並存造成錯誤。","observationEn":"Site practice: List camber values floor by floor in a versioned table; each monitoring-based update is issued by the structural engineer as a new revision, and surveyors set out only from the latest revision to avoid errors from coexisting versions.","failure":"注意干擾：預拱量若沿用設計預測而不依實測修正，實際沉陷較小時樓板會反向傾斜；預拱分配錯誤也可能讓帶狀桁架或外伸臂在鎖定時就承受非預期的初始力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying design-stage camber without updating for measured settlement leaves floors sloping the other way if real settlement is smaller; misallocated camber can also load belt trusses or outriggers with unintended initial forces at the time of locking. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在筏基頂面與核心筒、巨柱腳設置沉陷觀測點，每增加若干樓層量測一次，與預測曲線比較並修正後續樓層的預拱值；完工後以全樓層標高測量確認樓板平整度。","textEn":"Install settlement points on the mat top, core and mega-column bases, survey them after every few storeys, compare with the predicted curve and adjust camber for later floors; after completion confirm floor levelness with a full-height level survey.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"預拱值應以表格逐層列出並標註版本，每次依監測更新時由結構工程師發布新版，測量團隊只依最新版放樣，避免多版本並存造成錯誤。","textEn":"List camber values floor by floor in a versioned table; each monitoring-based update is issued by the structural engineer as a new revision, and surveyors set out only from the latest revision to avoid errors from coexisting versions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「差異沉陷的預拱補償」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Camber compensation for differential settlement\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。","在筏基頂面與核心筒、巨柱腳設置沉陷觀測點，每增加若干樓層量測一次，與預測曲線比較並修正後續樓層的預拱值；完工後以全樓層標高測量確認樓板平整度。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues.","Install settlement points on the mat top, core and mega-column bases, survey them after every few storeys, compare with the predicted curve and adjust camber for later floors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在筏基頂面與核心筒、巨柱腳設置沉陷觀測點，每增加若干樓層量測一次，與預測曲線比較並修正後續樓層的預拱值；完工後以全樓層標高測量確認樓板平整度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Install settlement points on the mat top, core and mega-column bases, survey them after every few storeys, compare with the predicted curve and adjust camber for later floors; after completion confirm floor levelness with a full-height level survey. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b027-v13-24","title":"差異沉陷的預拱補償：失效診斷","titleEn":"Camber compensation for differential settlement: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「巨柱垂直預拱」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vertical camber of mega-columns” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"預拱量若沿用設計預測而不依實測修正，實際沉陷較小時樓板會反向傾斜；預拱分配錯誤也可能讓帶狀桁架或外伸臂在鎖定時就承受非預期的初始力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying design-stage camber without updating for measured settlement leaves floors sloping the other way if real settlement is smaller; misallocated camber can also load belt trusses or outriggers with unintended initial forces at the time of locking. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：預拱量來自地盤—筏基互制分析與施工順序，並在施工中依實測沉陷修正；若不預拱，周邊樓板會相對核心筒下傾，影響樓板排水、帷幕牆接縫與電梯門檻。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The camber comes from soil–mat interaction analysis and the construction sequence and is updated with measured settlements; without it, perimeter floors would slope down relative to the core, affecting floor drainage, façade joints and elevator sills.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"預拱量若沿用設計預測而不依實測修正，實際沉陷較小時樓板會反向傾斜；預拱分配錯誤也可能讓帶狀桁架或外伸臂在鎖定時就承受非預期的初始力。","textEn":"Applying design-stage camber without updating for measured settlement leaves floors sloping the other way if real settlement is smaller; misallocated camber can also load belt trusses or outriggers with unintended initial forces at the time of locking.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「差異沉陷的預拱補償」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Camber compensation for differential settlement\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["預拱量若沿用設計預測而不依實測修正，實際沉陷較小時樓板會反向傾斜；預拱分配錯誤也可能讓帶狀桁架或外伸臂在鎖定時就承受非預期的初始力。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。"],"optionsEn":["Applying design-stage camber without updating for measured settlement leaves floors sloping the other way if real settlement is smaller.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"預拱量若沿用設計預測而不依實測修正，實際沉陷較小時樓板會反向傾斜；預拱分配錯誤也可能讓帶狀桁架或外伸臂在鎖定時就承受非預期的初始力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying design-stage camber without updating for measured settlement leaves floors sloping the other way if real settlement is smaller; misallocated camber can also load belt trusses or outriggers with unintended initial forces at the time of locking. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b027-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「施工中頻率量測與模型校準」與「地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction\" and \"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b027-v13-25","title":"施工中頻率量測與模型校準：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「施工期自然頻率量測」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Natural frequency during construction” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"設計單位公開說明，結構健康監測系統在施工期間與完工後量測自然頻率，並與分析模型比較。施工中結構的質量與勁度隨樓層、帷幕牆與裝修不斷改變，因此每個階段的實測頻率都是校正模型的機會：若頻率比預測高，表示實際勁度較高或質量較低；若偏低，則可能是混凝土模數、開裂或非結構質量與假設不同。提早校準可以修正完工後的加速度預測與阻尼需求判斷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「施工期自然頻率量測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The design team has stated that the structural health monitoring system measured natural frequencies during and after construction for comparison with analysis. Mass and stiffness change continually as floors, façade and fit-out are added, so each stage's measured frequency is a chance to calibrate the model: a higher frequency than predicted suggests higher stiffness or less mass, a lower one points to different concrete modulus, cracking or non-structural mass than assumed. Early calibration improves the prediction of in-service acceleration and of any damping need. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Natural frequency during construction” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：f = (1/2π)√(k/m)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: f = (1/2π)√(k/m).","failure":"常見誤解：「完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「施工期自然頻率量測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Natural frequency during construction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-25-k1","title":"施工中頻率量測與模型校準","titleEn":"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction","text":"設計單位公開說明，結構健康監測系統在施工期間與完工後量測自然頻率，並與分析模型比較。施工中結構的質量與勁度隨樓層、帷幕牆與裝修不斷改變，因此每個階段的實測頻率都是校正模型的機會：若頻率比預測高，表示實際勁度較高或質量較低；若偏低，則可能是混凝土模數、開裂或非結構質量與假設不同。","textEn":"The design team has stated that the structural health monitoring system measured natural frequencies during and after construction for comparison with analysis. Mass and stiffness change continually as floors, façade and fit-out are added, so each stage's measured frequency is a chance to calibrate the model: a higher frequency than predicted suggests higher stiffness or less mass, a lower one points to different concrete modulus, cracking or non-structural mass than assumed.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「施工中頻率量測與模型校準」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction\" is correct?","options":["完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。","設計單位公開說明，結構健康監測系統在施工期間與完工後量測自然頻率，並與分析模型比較。","樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。"],"optionsEn":["A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model.","The design team has stated that the structural health monitoring system measured natural frequencies during and after construction for comparison with analysis.","Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設計單位公開說明，結構健康監測系統在施工期間與完工後量測自然頻率，並與分析模型比較。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The design team has stated that the structural health monitoring system measured natural frequencies during and after construction for comparison with analysis. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b027-v13-26","title":"施工中頻率量測與模型校準：定量估算","titleEn":"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「施工期自然頻率量測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Natural frequency during construction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：f = (1/2π)√(k/m)。勁度不變、質量因帷幕牆與裝修增加 25% 時，f₂/f₁ = 1/√1.25 ≈ 0.894；若結構體完成時實測 f₁ = 0.125 Hz，完工後預期約 0.112 Hz。若完工實測為 0.118 Hz，代表質量增量或勁度假設需要修正。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: f = (1/2π)√(k/m). With unchanged stiffness and a 25% mass increase from façade and fit-out, f₂/f₁ = 1/√1.25 ≈ 0.894; a measured f₁ = 0.125 Hz at frame completion predicts about 0.112 Hz at handover. A measured 0.118 Hz would mean the mass increment or stiffness assumption needs correcting. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：於核心筒頂與數個中間樓層設置雙向加速度計，在低風時段做環境振動量測，以頻域分解辨識前三個模態；每次量測都記錄當時的樓層數、帷幕牆與裝修完成度，與同一施工狀態的模型比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Place biaxial accelerometers at the top of the core and several intermediate levels, take ambient measurements in calm periods and identify the first three modes by frequency-domain decomposition; record the number of floors and the extent of façade and fit-out at each measurement and compare with a model of the same construction state.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"f = (1/2π)√(k/m)。勁度不變、質量因帷幕牆與裝修增加 25% 時，f₂/f₁ = 1/√1.25 ≈ 0.894；若結構體完成時實測 f₁ = 0.125 Hz，完工後預期約 0.112 Hz。若完工實測為 0.118 Hz，代表質量增量或勁度假設需要修正。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"f = (1/2π)√(k/m). With unchanged stiffness and a 25% mass increase from façade and fit-out, f₂/f₁ = 1/√1.25 ≈ 0.894; a measured f₁ = 0.125 Hz at frame completion predicts about 0.112 Hz at handover. A measured 0.118 Hz would mean the mass increment or stiffness assumption needs correcting. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「施工中頻率量測與模型校準」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction\", which statement holds?","options":["感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。","外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。","f = (1/2π)√(k/m)。"],"optionsEn":["More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance.","More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better.","f = (1/2π)√(k/m)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"f = (1/2π)√(k/m)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"f = (1/2π)√(k/m). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b027-v13-27","title":"施工中頻率量測與模型校準：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「施工期自然頻率量測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Natural frequency during construction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"於核心筒頂與數個中間樓層設置雙向加速度計，在低風時段做環境振動量測，以頻域分解辨識前三個模態；每次量測都記錄當時的樓層數、帷幕牆與裝修完成度，與同一施工狀態的模型比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Place biaxial accelerometers at the top of the core and several intermediate levels, take ambient measurements in calm periods and identify the first three modes by frequency-domain decomposition; record the number of floors and the extent of façade and fit-out at each measurement and compare with a model of the same construction state. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：監測計畫要規定施工中量測的樓層節點與當時需同步記錄的施工狀態，並由結構顧問在每次量測後出具校準結論，作為後續預拱、加速度預測與交接基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: The monitoring plan should define the construction milestones for measurement and the construction state to record alongside, with the structural consultant issuing a calibration conclusion after each measurement as the basis for camber, acceleration prediction and the handover baseline.","failure":"注意干擾：若只在完工後量一次頻率，與模型差異的原因無法分辨是勁度還是質量；以錯誤的模型推估加速度，可能低估居住性問題或高估需要的阻尼措施。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Measuring frequency only once after completion leaves it impossible to tell whether a mismatch comes from stiffness or mass; predicting acceleration from a wrong model can underestimate habitability problems or overestimate the damping needed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"於核心筒頂與數個中間樓層設置雙向加速度計，在低風時段做環境振動量測，以頻域分解辨識前三個模態；每次量測都記錄當時的樓層數、帷幕牆與裝修完成度，與同一施工狀態的模型比較。","textEn":"Place biaxial accelerometers at the top of the core and several intermediate levels, take ambient measurements in calm periods and identify the first three modes by frequency-domain decomposition; record the number of floors and the extent of façade and fit-out at each measurement and compare with a model of the same construction state.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"監測計畫要規定施工中量測的樓層節點與當時需同步記錄的施工狀態，並由結構顧問在每次量測後出具校準結論，作為後續預拱、加速度預測與交接基準。","textEn":"The monitoring plan should define the construction milestones for measurement and the construction state to record alongside, with the structural consultant issuing a calibration conclusion after each measurement as the basis for camber, acceleration prediction and the handover baseline.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「施工中頻率量測與模型校準」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction\"?","options":["於核心筒頂與數個中間樓層設置雙向加速度計，在低風時段做環境振動量測，以頻域分解辨識前三個模態。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["Place biaxial accelerometers at the top of the core and several intermediate levels, take ambient measurements in calm periods and identify the first three modes by frequency-domain decomposition.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect."],"answer":0,"explanation":"於核心筒頂與數個中間樓層設置雙向加速度計，在低風時段做環境振動量測，以頻域分解辨識前三個模態；每次量測都記錄當時的樓層數、帷幕牆與裝修完成度，與同一施工狀態的模型比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Place biaxial accelerometers at the top of the core and several intermediate levels, take ambient measurements in calm periods and identify the first three modes by frequency-domain decomposition; record the number of floors and the extent of façade and fit-out at each measurement and compare with a model of the same construction state. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b027-v13-28","title":"施工中頻率量測與模型校準：失效診斷","titleEn":"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「施工期自然頻率量測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Natural frequency during construction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只在完工後量一次頻率，與模型差異的原因無法分辨是勁度還是質量；以錯誤的模型推估加速度，可能低估居住性問題或高估需要的阻尼措施。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Measuring frequency only once after completion leaves it impossible to tell whether a mismatch comes from stiffness or mass; predicting acceleration from a wrong model can underestimate habitability problems or overestimate the damping needed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：提早校準可以修正完工後的加速度預測與阻尼需求判斷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Early calibration improves the prediction of in-service acceleration and of any damping need.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只在完工後量一次頻率，與模型差異的原因無法分辨是勁度還是質量；以錯誤的模型推估加速度，可能低估居住性問題或高估需要的阻尼措施。","textEn":"Measuring frequency only once after completion leaves it impossible to tell whether a mismatch comes from stiffness or mass; predicting acceleration from a wrong model can underestimate habitability problems or overestimate the damping needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「施工中頻率量測與模型校準」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Frequency measurement and model calibration during construction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若只在完工後量一次頻率，與模型差異的原因無法分辨是勁度還是質量；以錯誤的模型推估加速度，可能低估居住性問題或高估需要的阻尼措施。","樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Measuring frequency only once after completion leaves it impossible to tell whether a mismatch comes from stiffness or mass.","Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若只在完工後量一次頻率，與模型差異的原因無法分辨是勁度還是質量；以錯誤的模型推估加速度，可能低估居住性問題或高估需要的阻尼措施。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Measuring frequency only once after completion leaves it impossible to tell whether a mismatch comes from stiffness or mass; predicting acceleration from a wrong model can underestimate habitability problems or overestimate the damping needed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b027-v13-29","title":"地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「斷層帶補強樁與筏基沉陷」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fault-zone reinforcing piles and mat settlement” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"筏基主要坐落在岩盤上，設計容許承壓約 3,000 kPa；在斷層與剪裂帶，以衝擊旋轉鑽掘（PRD）施作直徑約 1.0 m 的補強樁改良地盤，官方資料稱共 108 根、長約 30 m。依當地法規，這些樁不與筏基相連，樁頂與筏基間以砂墊層隔開，所以它們提高的是地盤勁度，而不是當作傳統樁基礎直接承載柱力。設計以靜態與動態地盤彈簧模擬筏基，使不同區域的勁度差異反映在沉陷與筏基內力中。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「斷層帶補強樁與筏基沉陷」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The mat bears mainly on rock with an allowable bearing pressure of about 3,000 kPa; in fault and shear zones the ground was reinforced with piles about 1.0 m in diameter installed by percussion rotary drilling, reported officially as 108 piles about 30 m long. Under local regulations the piles are not connected to the mat and a sand cushion separates their tops from it, so they stiffen the ground rather than carry column loads directly as a conventional pile foundation. The mat was modelled on static and dynamic soil springs so stiffness differences between zones appear in settlement and mat forces. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Fault-zone reinforcing piles and mat settlement” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以地盤反力係數估算沉陷 s = q/k_s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Estimate settlement with a subgrade modulus, s = q/k_s.","failure":"常見誤解：「樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「斷層帶補強樁與筏基沉陷」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Fault-zone reinforcing piles and mat settlement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-29-k1","title":"地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證","titleEn":"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification","text":"筏基主要坐落在岩盤上，設計容許承壓約 3,000 kPa；在斷層與剪裂帶，以衝擊旋轉鑽掘（PRD）施作直徑約 1.0 m 的補強樁改良地盤，官方資料稱共 108 根、長約 30 m。依當地法規，這些樁不與筏基相連，樁頂與筏基間以砂墊層隔開，所以它們提高的是地盤勁度，而不是當作傳統樁基礎直接承載柱力。","textEn":"The mat bears mainly on rock with an allowable bearing pressure of about 3,000 kPa; in fault and shear zones the ground was reinforced with piles about 1.0 m in diameter installed by percussion rotary drilling, reported officially as 108 piles about 30 m long. Under local regulations the piles are not connected to the mat and a sand cushion separates their tops from it, so they stiffen the ground rather than carry column loads directly as a conventional pile foundation.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification\" is correct?","options":["樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。","外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。","筏基主要坐落在岩盤上，設計容許承壓約 3,000 kPa。"],"optionsEn":["Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat.","Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change.","The mat bears mainly on rock with an allowable bearing pressure of about 3,000 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"筏基主要坐落在岩盤上，設計容許承壓約 3,000 kPa；在斷層與剪裂帶，以衝擊旋轉鑽掘（PRD）施作直徑約 1.0 m 的補強樁改良地盤，官方資料稱共 108 根、長約 30 m。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The mat bears mainly on rock with an allowable bearing pressure of about 3,000 kPa; in fault and shear zones the ground was reinforced with piles about 1.0 m in diameter installed by percussion rotary drilling, reported officially as 108 piles about 30 m long. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b027-v13-30","title":"地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「斷層帶補強樁與筏基沉陷」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fault-zone reinforcing piles and mat settlement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以地盤反力係數估算沉陷 s = q/k_s。接觸壓力 q = 1,400 kPa：岩盤區 k_s = 150 MN/m³ 時 s ≈ 9.3 mm；未補強的斷層帶 k_s = 50 MN/m³ 時 s = 28 mm，兩區相差約 19 mm。補強樁若把斷層帶 k_s 提高到 120 MN/m³，s ≈ 11.7 mm，差異降到約 2.3 mm。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Estimate settlement with a subgrade modulus, s = q/k_s. For a contact pressure q = 1,400 kPa, rock zones with k_s = 150 MN/m³ settle about 9.3 mm, while an unimproved fault zone with k_s = 50 MN/m³ settles 28 mm, about 19 mm more. If reinforcing piles raise the fault-zone k_s to 120 MN/m³, s ≈ 11.7 mm and the difference falls to about 2.3 mm. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：補強樁施工後以鑽心或非破壞試驗確認樁身完整性，並以平鈑載重或孔內試驗量測改良後地盤勁度；筏基施工後在斷層帶與岩盤區分別設置沉陷點，比較實測差異沉陷與分析值。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After installing the reinforcing piles, confirm shaft integrity by coring or non-destructive testing and measure improved ground stiffness with plate-load or borehole tests; after the mat is cast, set settlement points over fault and rock zones and compare measured differential settlement with the analysis.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以地盤反力係數估算沉陷 s = q/k_s。接觸壓力 q = 1,400 kPa：岩盤區 k_s = 150 MN/m³ 時 s ≈ 9.3 mm；未補強的斷層帶 k_s = 50 MN/m³ 時 s = 28 mm，兩區相差約 19 mm。補強樁若把斷層帶 k_s 提高到 120 MN/m³，s ≈ 11.7 mm，差異降到約 2.3 mm。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Estimate settlement with a subgrade modulus, s = q/k_s. For a contact pressure q = 1,400 kPa, rock zones with k_s = 150 MN/m³ settle about 9.3 mm, while an unimproved fault zone with k_s = 50 MN/m³ settles 28 mm, about 19 mm more. If reinforcing piles raise the fault-zone k_s to 120 MN/m³, s ≈ 11.7 mm and the difference falls to about 2.3 mm. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification\", which statement holds?","options":["以地盤反力係數估算沉陷 s = q/k_s。","核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。","巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。"],"optionsEn":["Estimate settlement with a subgrade modulus, s = q/k_s.","The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas.","A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以地盤反力係數估算沉陷 s = q/k_s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Estimate settlement with a subgrade modulus, s = q/k_s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b027-v13-31","title":"地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「斷層帶補強樁與筏基沉陷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fault-zone reinforcing piles and mat settlement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"補強樁施工後以鑽心或非破壞試驗確認樁身完整性，並以平鈑載重或孔內試驗量測改良後地盤勁度；筏基施工後在斷層帶與岩盤區分別設置沉陷點，比較實測差異沉陷與分析值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After installing the reinforcing piles, confirm shaft integrity by coring or non-destructive testing and measure improved ground stiffness with plate-load or borehole tests; after the mat is cast, set settlement points over fault and rock zones and compare measured differential settlement with the analysis. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：補強樁與砂墊層的施工須列入檢驗停留點，包含樁頂高程、墊層厚度與壓實度；地質調查報告與實際開挖揭露的斷層位置要互相比對並由大地工程師簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Make reinforcing piles and the sand cushion hold points covering pile-top level, cushion thickness and compaction, and have the geotechnical engineer reconcile and sign off the fault locations in the investigation report against those revealed by excavation.","failure":"注意干擾：若斷層帶範圍調查不足，筏基某一角落的沉陷可能明顯大於預測，造成筏基彎矩重分配與上部結構差異變位；樁頂若未依設計與筏基隔開，樁會吸收集中荷載而在筏基內形成未預期的衝剪。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the fault zone is poorly mapped, one corner of the mat can settle much more than predicted, redistributing mat moments and adding differential movement to the superstructure; if pile tops are not separated from the mat as designed, the piles attract concentrated loads and create unexpected punching shear in the mat. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"補強樁施工後以鑽心或非破壞試驗確認樁身完整性，並以平鈑載重或孔內試驗量測改良後地盤勁度；筏基施工後在斷層帶與岩盤區分別設置沉陷點，比較實測差異沉陷與分析值。","textEn":"After installing the reinforcing piles, confirm shaft integrity by coring or non-destructive testing and measure improved ground stiffness with plate-load or borehole tests; after the mat is cast, set settlement points over fault and rock zones and compare measured differential settlement with the analysis.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"補強樁與砂墊層的施工須列入檢驗停留點，包含樁頂高程、墊層厚度與壓實度；地質調查報告與實際開挖揭露的斷層位置要互相比對並由大地工程師簽認。","textEn":"Make reinforcing piles and the sand cushion hold points covering pile-top level, cushion thickness and compaction, and have the geotechnical engineer reconcile and sign off the fault locations in the investigation report against those revealed by excavation.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","補強樁施工後以鑽心或非破壞試驗確認樁身完整性，並以平鈑載重或孔內試驗量測改良後地盤勁度；筏基施工後在斷層帶與岩盤區分別設置沉陷點，比較實測差異沉陷與分析值。","巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","After installing the reinforcing piles, confirm shaft integrity by coring or non-destructive testing and measure improved ground stiffness with plate-load or borehole tests.","If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference."],"answer":1,"explanation":"補強樁施工後以鑽心或非破壞試驗確認樁身完整性，並以平鈑載重或孔內試驗量測改良後地盤勁度；筏基施工後在斷層帶與岩盤區分別設置沉陷點，比較實測差異沉陷與分析值。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After installing the reinforcing piles, confirm shaft integrity by coring or non-destructive testing and measure improved ground stiffness with plate-load or borehole tests; after the mat is cast, set settlement points over fault and rock zones and compare measured differential settlement with the analysis. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b027-v13-32","title":"地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「斷層帶補強樁與筏基沉陷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fault-zone reinforcing piles and mat settlement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若斷層帶範圍調查不足，筏基某一角落的沉陷可能明顯大於預測，造成筏基彎矩重分配與上部結構差異變位；樁頂若未依設計與筏基隔開，樁會吸收集中荷載而在筏基內形成未預期的衝剪。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the fault zone is poorly mapped, one corner of the mat can settle much more than predicted, redistributing mat moments and adding differential movement to the superstructure; if pile tops are not separated from the mat as designed, the piles attract concentrated loads and create unexpected punching shear in the mat. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：設計以靜態與動態地盤彈簧模擬筏基，使不同區域的勁度差異反映在沉陷與筏基內力中。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The mat was modelled on static and dynamic soil springs so stiffness differences between zones appear in settlement and mat forces.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「樁一定要與筏基連結才能發揮作用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Piles only work if they are structurally connected to the mat.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若斷層帶範圍調查不足，筏基某一角落的沉陷可能明顯大於預測，造成筏基彎矩重分配與上部結構差異變位；樁頂若未依設計與筏基隔開，樁會吸收集中荷載而在筏基內形成未預期的衝剪。","textEn":"If the fault zone is poorly mapped, one corner of the mat can settle much more than predicted, redistributing mat moments and adding differential movement to the superstructure; if pile tops are not separated from the mat as designed, the piles attract concentrated loads and create unexpected punching shear in the mat.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地盤補強樁與沉陷驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ground-reinforcing piles and settlement verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。","若斷層帶範圍調查不足，筏基某一角落的沉陷可能明顯大於預測，造成筏基彎矩重分配與上部結構差異變位。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change.","If the fault zone is poorly mapped, one corner of the mat can settle much more than predicted, redistributing mat moments and adding differential movement to the superstructure."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若斷層帶範圍調查不足，筏基某一角落的沉陷可能明顯大於預測，造成筏基彎矩重分配與上部結構差異變位；樁頂若未依設計與筏基隔開，樁會吸收集中荷載而在筏基內形成未預期的衝剪。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the fault zone is poorly mapped, one corner of the mat can settle much more than predicted, redistributing mat moments and adding differential movement to the superstructure; if pile tops are not separated from the mat as designed, the piles attract concentrated loads and create unexpected punching shear in the mat. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b027-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量」與「結構健康監測與營運交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces\" and \"Structural health monitoring and operational handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b027-v13-33","title":"潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「外伸臂長期力量轉移」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long-term outrigger force transfer” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"外伸臂鎖定後，核心筒與巨柱之間仍持續發生潛變與收縮造成的差異縮短，這部分位移會被外伸臂桁架抵抗，轉成斜桿與接頭中的長期軸力，並把荷重在核心與巨柱間重新分配。設計者因此建議延後外伸臂最終接合，並針對長期力量轉移設計構件。鎖定越晚，鎖定後剩下的差異縮短越少，外伸臂承受的附加力也越小，但施工期間就得依靠其他系統提供側向勁度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「外伸臂長期力量轉移」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"After outriggers are locked, creep and shrinkage keep producing differential shortening between core and mega-columns; the outrigger trusses resist that movement, turning it into long-term axial forces in diagonals and joints and redistributing load between core and columns. The designers therefore recommended delaying the final outrigger connections and designing members for long-term force transfer. The later the locking, the less differential shortening remains and the smaller the added force, but lateral stiffness during construction must then come from other systems. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Long-term outrigger force transfer” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：附加力 F = k·δ_post。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The added force is F = k·δ_post.","failure":"常見誤解：「外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「外伸臂長期力量轉移」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Long-term outrigger force transfer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-33-k1","title":"潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量","titleEn":"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces","text":"外伸臂鎖定後，核心筒與巨柱之間仍持續發生潛變與收縮造成的差異縮短，這部分位移會被外伸臂桁架抵抗，轉成斜桿與接頭中的長期軸力，並把荷重在核心與巨柱間重新分配。設計者因此建議延後外伸臂最終接合，並針對長期力量轉移設計構件。","textEn":"After outriggers are locked, creep and shrinkage keep producing differential shortening between core and mega-columns; the outrigger trusses resist that movement, turning it into long-term axial forces in diagonals and joints and redistributing load between core and columns. The designers therefore recommended delaying the final outrigger connections and designing members for long-term force transfer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces\" is correct?","options":["外伸臂鎖定後，核心筒與巨柱之間仍持續發生潛變與收縮造成的差異縮短，這部分位移會被外伸臂桁架抵抗，轉成斜桿與接頭中的長期軸力，並把荷重在核心與巨柱間重新分配。","外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。","感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。"],"optionsEn":["After outriggers are locked, creep and shrinkage keep producing differential shortening between core and mega-columns.","Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change.","More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外伸臂鎖定後，核心筒與巨柱之間仍持續發生潛變與收縮造成的差異縮短，這部分位移會被外伸臂桁架抵抗，轉成斜桿與接頭中的長期軸力，並把荷重在核心與巨柱間重新分配。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"After outriggers are locked, creep and shrinkage keep producing differential shortening between core and mega-columns; the outrigger trusses resist that movement, turning it into long-term axial forces in diagonals and joints and redistributing load between core and columns. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b027-v13-34","title":"潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量：定量估算","titleEn":"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「外伸臂長期力量轉移」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long-term outrigger force transfer” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：附加力 F = k·δ_post。外伸臂等效垂直勁度 k = 800 kN/mm：若鎖定後剩餘差異縮短 δ_post = 12 mm，F = 9,600 kN；若提早在結構只完成一半時鎖定，δ_post = 30 mm，F = 24,000 kN，增加 2.5 倍。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The added force is F = k·δ_post. With an equivalent vertical outrigger stiffness k = 800 kN/mm, a residual differential shortening after locking of δ_post = 12 mm gives F = 9,600 kN; locking early with only half the structure complete leaves δ_post = 30 mm and F = 24,000 kN, 2.5 times more. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以施工階段與時間相依分析預測不同鎖定時點的外伸臂力，選擇鎖定時點後在斜桿上設置應變計長期記錄，比對實測軸力增長與預測曲線，偏離過大時檢討潛變參數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use construction-stage, time-dependent analysis to predict outrigger forces for different locking times; after choosing one, install strain gauges on the diagonals for long-term recording, compare measured force growth with the prediction and revisit creep parameters if they diverge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"附加力 F = k·δ_post。外伸臂等效垂直勁度 k = 800 kN/mm：若鎖定後剩餘差異縮短 δ_post = 12 mm，F = 9,600 kN；若提早在結構只完成一半時鎖定，δ_post = 30 mm，F = 24,000 kN，增加 2.5 倍。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"The added force is F = k·δ_post. With an equivalent vertical outrigger stiffness k = 800 kN/mm, a residual differential shortening after locking of δ_post = 12 mm gives F = 9,600 kN; locking early with only half the structure complete leaves δ_post = 30 mm and F = 24,000 kN, 2.5 times more. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces\", which statement holds?","options":["外伸臂越多、越剛，結構表現就一定越好。","附加力 F = k·δ_post。","延遲接合只是施工方便，對結構受力沒有影響。"],"optionsEn":["More and stiffer outriggers always make the structure perform better.","The added force is F = k·δ_post.","Delayed connection is only a construction convenience with no structural effect."],"answer":1,"explanation":"附加力 F = k·δ_post。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The added force is F = k·δ_post. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b027-v13-35","title":"潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「外伸臂長期力量轉移」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long-term outrigger force transfer” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以施工階段與時間相依分析預測不同鎖定時點的外伸臂力，選擇鎖定時點後在斜桿上設置應變計長期記錄，比對實測軸力增長與預測曲線，偏離過大時檢討潛變參數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use construction-stage, time-dependent analysis to predict outrigger forces for different locking times; after choosing one, install strain gauges on the diagonals for long-term recording, compare measured force growth with the prediction and revisit creep parameters if they diverge. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應記錄外伸臂鎖定日期、當時的樓層與荷重狀態、預測長期力量曲線與監測基準，並規定定期比對；接頭應設計成可檢查，必要時可調整或補強。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents should record the outrigger locking date, the floors and load state at that time, the predicted long-term force curve and monitoring baseline, with periodic comparison required; joints should be inspectable and adjustable or strengthenable if needed.","failure":"注意干擾：若沒有考慮長期力量轉移，外伸臂接頭可能在完工數年後因持續累積的軸力而出現螺栓滑移或焊道裂縫；核心筒牆體在外伸臂連接處也可能出現局部開裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Without allowing for long-term force transfer, outrigger joints may suffer bolt slip or weld cracking years after completion as axial force keeps accumulating, and core walls may crack locally at outrigger connections. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以施工階段與時間相依分析預測不同鎖定時點的外伸臂力，選擇鎖定時點後在斜桿上設置應變計長期記錄，比對實測軸力增長與預測曲線，偏離過大時檢討潛變參數。","textEn":"Use construction-stage, time-dependent analysis to predict outrigger forces for different locking times; after choosing one, install strain gauges on the diagonals for long-term recording, compare measured force growth with the prediction and revisit creep parameters if they diverge.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應記錄外伸臂鎖定日期、當時的樓層與荷重狀態、預測長期力量曲線與監測基準，並規定定期比對；接頭應設計成可檢查，必要時可調整或補強。","textEn":"Handover documents should record the outrigger locking date, the floors and load state at that time, the predicted long-term force curve and monitoring baseline, with periodic comparison required; joints should be inspectable and adjustable or strengthenable if needed.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","筏基夠厚就會整體均勻沉陷，不需要考慮差異沉陷。","以施工階段與時間相依分析預測不同鎖定時點的外伸臂力，選擇鎖定時點後在斜桿上設置應變計長期記錄，比對實測軸力增長與預測曲線，偏離過大時檢討潛變參數。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A thick enough mat settles uniformly, so differential settlement can be ignored.","Use construction-stage, time-dependent analysis to predict outrigger forces for different locking times."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以施工階段與時間相依分析預測不同鎖定時點的外伸臂力，選擇鎖定時點後在斜桿上設置應變計長期記錄，比對實測軸力增長與預測曲線，偏離過大時檢討潛變參數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use construction-stage, time-dependent analysis to predict outrigger forces for different locking times; after choosing one, install strain gauges on the diagonals for long-term recording, compare measured force growth with the prediction and revisit creep parameters if they diverge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b027-v13-36","title":"潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「外伸臂長期力量轉移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long-term outrigger force transfer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若沒有考慮長期力量轉移，外伸臂接頭可能在完工數年後因持續累積的軸力而出現螺栓滑移或焊道裂縫；核心筒牆體在外伸臂連接處也可能出現局部開裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Without allowing for long-term force transfer, outrigger joints may suffer bolt slip or weld cracking years after completion as axial force keeps accumulating, and core walls may crack locally at outrigger connections. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鎖定越晚，鎖定後剩下的差異縮短越少，外伸臂承受的附加力也越小，但施工期間就得依靠其他系統提供側向勁度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The later the locking, the less differential shortening remains and the smaller the added force, but lateral stiffness during construction must then come from other systems.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「外伸臂鎖定後，其中的力量就固定不再變化。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once outriggers are locked, the forces in them no longer change.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若沒有考慮長期力量轉移，外伸臂接頭可能在完工數年後因持續累積的軸力而出現螺栓滑移或焊道裂縫；核心筒牆體在外伸臂連接處也可能出現局部開裂。","textEn":"Without allowing for long-term force transfer, outrigger joints may suffer bolt slip or weld cracking years after completion as axial force keeps accumulating, and core walls may crack locally at outrigger connections.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「潛變收縮與外伸臂的長期力量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Creep, shrinkage and long-term outrigger forces\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若沒有考慮長期力量轉移，外伸臂接頭可能在完工數年後因持續累積的軸力而出現螺栓滑移或焊道裂縫；核心筒牆體在外伸臂連接處也可能出現局部開裂。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。"],"optionsEn":["Without allowing for long-term force transfer, outrigger joints may suffer bolt slip or weld cracking years after completion as axial force keeps accumulating, and core walls may crack locally at outrigger connections.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若沒有考慮長期力量轉移，外伸臂接頭可能在完工數年後因持續累積的軸力而出現螺栓滑移或焊道裂縫；核心筒牆體在外伸臂連接處也可能出現局部開裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Without allowing for long-term force transfer, outrigger joints may suffer bolt slip or weld cracking years after completion as axial force keeps accumulating, and core walls may crack locally at outrigger connections. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b027-v13-37","title":"結構健康監測與營運交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Structural health monitoring and operational handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「600 個感測器的健康監測」如何影響樂天世界塔的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Health monitoring with 600 sensors” governs force, deformation or durability in “Lotte World Tower”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"官方資料指出塔內設有超過 600 個感測器的結構健康監測系統，即時監看颱風、地震與其他風險；設計論文提到量測項目包括風荷載、應力、位移、加速度、傾斜與現場反應，並以有限元素模擬輔助判讀。監測的價值在於建立基準：交接時的頻率、傾斜、應力與沉陷基準，讓事件後能以數據判斷結構是否仍在預期行為範圍內，並作為營運單位決定是否需要檢查或限制使用的依據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「600 個感測器的健康監測」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Official sources say the tower has a structural health monitoring system of more than 600 sensors watching typhoon, earthquake and other risks in real time; the design paper lists wind loads, stresses, displacements, accelerations, tilt and field response, interpreted with finite-element simulation. Monitoring is valuable because it sets baselines: handover values of frequency, tilt, stress and settlement let engineers judge after an event whether the structure is still behaving as expected, and give the operator a basis for deciding whether to inspect or restrict use. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Health monitoring with 600 sensors” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：基礎傾斜換算頂部變位 Δ = θ·H。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Foundation tilt converts to top displacement as Δ = θ·H.","failure":"常見誤解：「感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「600 個感測器的健康監測」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Health monitoring with 600 sensors”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-37-k1","title":"結構健康監測與營運交接","titleEn":"Structural health monitoring and operational handover","text":"官方資料指出塔內設有超過 600 個感測器的結構健康監測系統，即時監看颱風、地震與其他風險；設計論文提到量測項目包括風荷載、應力、位移、加速度、傾斜與現場反應，並以有限元素模擬輔助判讀。監測的價值在於建立基準：交接時的頻率、傾斜、應力與沉陷基準，讓事件後能以數據判斷結構是否仍在預期行為範圍內，並作為營運單位決定是否需要檢查或限制使用的依據。","textEn":"Official sources say the tower has a structural health monitoring system of more than 600 sensors watching typhoon, earthquake and other risks in real time; the design paper lists wind loads, stresses, displacements, accelerations, tilt and field response, interpreted with finite-element simulation. Monitoring is valuable because it sets baselines: handover values of frequency, tilt, stress and settlement let engineers judge after an event whether the structure is still behaving as expected, and give the operator a basis for deciding whether to inspect or restrict use.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「結構健康監測與營運交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Structural health monitoring and operational handover\" is correct?","options":["感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。","官方資料指出塔內設有超過 600 個感測器的結構健康監測系統，即時監看颱風、地震與其他風險。","核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。"],"optionsEn":["More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance.","Official sources say the tower has a structural health monitoring system of more than 600 sensors watching typhoon, earthquake and other risks in real time.","The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"官方資料指出塔內設有超過 600 個感測器的結構健康監測系統，即時監看颱風、地震與其他風險；設計論文提到量測項目包括風荷載、應力、位移、加速度、傾斜與現場反應，並以有限元素模擬輔助判讀。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Official sources say the tower has a structural health monitoring system of more than 600 sensors watching typhoon, earthquake and other risks in real time; the design paper lists wind loads, stresses, displacements, accelerations, tilt and field response, interpreted with finite-element simulation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b027-v13-38","title":"結構健康監測與營運交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Structural health monitoring and operational handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「600 個感測器的健康監測」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Health monitoring with 600 sensors” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：基礎傾斜換算頂部變位 Δ = θ·H。若筏基傾斜計讀到 θ = 1×10⁻⁴ rad，對 H = 554.5 m 的塔，剛體轉動造成的頂部位移 Δ = 1×10⁻⁴×554,500 ≈ 55 mm。因此傾斜計的漂移或溫度效應若達 0.5×10⁻⁴ rad，就足以在頂部造成約 28 mm 的誤判。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Foundation tilt converts to top displacement as Δ = θ·H. A mat tiltmeter reading θ = 1×10⁻⁴ rad on an H = 554.5 m tower implies a rigid-body top displacement of Δ = 1×10⁻⁴×554,500 ≈ 55 mm. A tiltmeter drift or temperature effect of 0.5×10⁻⁴ rad would therefore misreport about 28 mm at the top. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：交接前完成感測器校正、溫度補償與資料品質檢查，並在低風時段建立頻率、傾斜與應變基準；訂定預警與行動門檻（例如頂部加速度、層間變位角與傾斜增量），每次事件後產出報告並與基準比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before handover finish sensor calibration, temperature compensation and data-quality checks, and set baselines for frequency, tilt and strain during calm periods; define alert and action thresholds such as top acceleration, inter-storey drift ratio and tilt increments, and produce an event report compared with the baseline after every event.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"基礎傾斜換算頂部變位 Δ = θ·H。若筏基傾斜計讀到 θ = 1×10⁻⁴ rad，對 H = 554.5 m 的塔，剛體轉動造成的頂部位移 Δ = 1×10⁻⁴×554,500 ≈ 55 mm。因此傾斜計的漂移或溫度效應若達 0.5×10⁻⁴ rad，就足以在頂部造成約 28 mm 的誤判。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Foundation tilt converts to top displacement as Δ = θ·H. A mat tiltmeter reading θ = 1×10⁻⁴ rad on an H = 554.5 m tower implies a rigid-body top displacement of Δ = 1×10⁻⁴×554,500 ≈ 55 mm. A tiltmeter drift or temperature effect of 0.5×10⁻⁴ rad would therefore misreport about 28 mm at the top. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「結構健康監測與營運交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Structural health monitoring and operational handover\", which statement holds?","options":["巨柱斷面巨大，所以不會有細長或挫屈問題。","巨厚筏基只要混凝土強度夠，分多次澆置與一次澆置沒有差別。","基礎傾斜換算頂部變位 Δ = θ·H。"],"optionsEn":["A huge mega-column is too big to have slenderness or buckling issues.","If the concrete is strong enough, pouring a massive mat in one go or in stages makes no difference.","Foundation tilt converts to top displacement as Δ = θ·H."],"answer":2,"explanation":"基礎傾斜換算頂部變位 Δ = θ·H。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Foundation tilt converts to top displacement as Δ = θ·H. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b027-v13-39","title":"結構健康監測與營運交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Structural health monitoring and operational handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「600 個感測器的健康監測」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Health monitoring with 600 sensors” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"交接前完成感測器校正、溫度補償與資料品質檢查，並在低風時段建立頻率、傾斜與應變基準；訂定預警與行動門檻（例如頂部加速度、層間變位角與傾斜增量），每次事件後產出報告並與基準比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before handover finish sensor calibration, temperature compensation and data-quality checks, and set baselines for frequency, tilt and strain during calm periods; define alert and action thresholds such as top acceleration, inter-storey drift ratio and tilt increments, and produce an event report compared with the baseline after every event. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件要包含感測器配置圖、校正紀錄、基準值、門檻與通報流程，並指定負責判讀的結構工程師與更換感測器的週期；營運單位每年檢討監測報告。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover documents must include the sensor layout, calibration records, baselines, thresholds and reporting procedure, naming the structural engineer responsible for interpretation and the sensor-replacement cycle; the operator reviews the monitoring report every year.","failure":"注意干擾：感測器長期無人維護時，漂移、斷線與時間不同步會讓資料失去判讀價值；若門檻未事先定義，事件後各方對資料的解讀可能不一致，延誤是否疏散或檢查的決策。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unmaintained sensors drift, lose connection and fall out of time sync until the data cannot be interpreted; without predefined thresholds, parties may read post-event data differently and delay decisions on evacuation or inspection. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"交接前完成感測器校正、溫度補償與資料品質檢查，並在低風時段建立頻率、傾斜與應變基準；訂定預警與行動門檻（例如頂部加速度、層間變位角與傾斜增量），每次事件後產出報告並與基準比較。","textEn":"Before handover finish sensor calibration, temperature compensation and data-quality checks, and set baselines for frequency, tilt and strain during calm periods; define alert and action thresholds such as top acceleration, inter-storey drift ratio and tilt increments, and produce an event report compared with the baseline after every event.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件要包含感測器配置圖、校正紀錄、基準值、門檻與通報流程，並指定負責判讀的結構工程師與更換感測器的週期；營運單位每年檢討監測報告。","textEn":"Handover documents must include the sensor layout, calibration records, baselines, thresholds and reporting procedure, naming the structural engineer responsible for interpretation and the sensor-replacement cycle; the operator reviews the monitoring report every year.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「結構健康監測與營運交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Structural health monitoring and operational handover\"?","options":["交接前完成感測器校正、溫度補償與資料品質檢查，並在低風時段建立頻率、傾斜與應變基準。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","完工後量一次頻率，就足以校準整個結構模型。"],"optionsEn":["Before handover finish sensor calibration, temperature compensation and data-quality checks, and set baselines for frequency, tilt and strain during calm periods.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A single frequency measurement after completion is enough to calibrate the whole structural model."],"answer":0,"explanation":"交接前完成感測器校正、溫度補償與資料品質檢查，並在低風時段建立頻率、傾斜與應變基準；訂定預警與行動門檻（例如頂部加速度、層間變位角與傾斜增量），每次事件後產出報告並與基準比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before handover finish sensor calibration, temperature compensation and data-quality checks, and set baselines for frequency, tilt and strain during calm periods; define alert and action thresholds such as top acceleration, inter-storey drift ratio and tilt increments, and produce an event report compared with the baseline after every event. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b027-v13-40","title":"結構健康監測與營運交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Structural health monitoring and operational handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"prerequisiteIds":["b027-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「600 個感測器的健康監測」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Health monitoring with 600 sensors” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"感測器長期無人維護時，漂移、斷線與時間不同步會讓資料失去判讀價值；若門檻未事先定義，事件後各方對資料的解讀可能不一致，延誤是否疏散或檢查的決策。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unmaintained sensors drift, lose connection and fall out of time sync until the data cannot be interpreted; without predefined thresholds, parties may read post-event data differently and delay decisions on evacuation or inspection. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：監測的價值在於建立基準：交接時的頻率、傾斜、應力與沉陷基準，讓事件後能以數據判斷結構是否仍在預期行為範圍內，並作為營運單位決定是否需要檢查或限制使用的依據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Monitoring is valuable because it sets baselines: handover values of frequency, tilt, stress and settlement let engineers judge after an event whether the structure is still behaving as expected, and give the operator a basis for deciding whether to inspect or restrict use.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「感測器越多，結構安全就越有保障，不需要人工判讀與維護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More sensors automatically mean a safer structure without human interpretation or maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b027-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"感測器長期無人維護時，漂移、斷線與時間不同步會讓資料失去判讀價值；若門檻未事先定義，事件後各方對資料的解讀可能不一致，延誤是否疏散或檢查的決策。","textEn":"Unmaintained sensors drift, lose connection and fall out of time sync until the data cannot be interpreted; without predefined thresholds, parties may read post-event data differently and delay decisions on evacuation or inspection.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]},{"id":"b027-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「結構健康監測與營運交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Structural health monitoring and operational handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","感測器長期無人維護時，漂移、斷線與時間不同步會讓資料失去判讀價值；若門檻未事先定義，事件後各方對資料的解讀可能不一致，延誤是否疏散或檢查的決策。","核心筒與巨柱的重力分擔完全由樓板受載面積決定。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unmaintained sensors drift, lose connection and fall out of time sync until the data cannot be interpreted.","The gravity split between core and mega-columns is set purely by tributary floor areas."],"answer":1,"explanation":"感測器長期無人維護時，漂移、斷線與時間不同步會讓資料失去判讀價值；若門檻未事先定義，事件後各方對資料的解讀可能不一致，延誤是否疏散或檢查的決策。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unmaintained sensors drift, lose connection and fall out of time sync until the data cannot be interpreted; without predefined thresholds, parties may read post-event data differently and delay decisions on evacuation or inspection. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-ctbuh-lotte-world-tower","v13s-ctbuh-paper-lotte-design","v13s-structure-mag-lotte","v13s-lotte-world-tower-official","v13s-enr-lotte-2011"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
